1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,362
Williams Obstetrics.

2
00:00:02,312 --> 00:00:05,987
Chapter 66: Neoplastic Disorders.

3
00:00:05,987 --> 00:00:14,175
Cancer Therapy In Pregnancy Cervix Uterus Ovary Breast Carcinoma BRCA1/2 MUTATIONS Thyroid Cancer.

4
00:00:14,175 --> 00:00:16,012
Lymphomas.

5
00:00:16,012 --> 00:00:18,187
Malignant Melanoma.

6
00:00:18,187 --> 00:00:21,075
Gastrointestinal Tract Cancer.

7
00:00:21,075 --> 00:00:22,837
References.

8
00:00:22,837 --> 00:00:28,700
Any of the many neoplasms that affect reproductive-aged women can complicate pregnancy.

9
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:36,850
Fortunately, most encountered neoplasms are benign, and uterine leiomyomas and ovarian cysts are the most frequent.

10
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:46,987
Despite this, the incidence of malignancy approximates 1 case per 1000 to 2000 pregnancies (Korenaga, 2020; Ma, 2020).

11
00:00:46,987 --> 00:00:52,475
A third are diagnosed prenatally, and the remainder within 12 months of delivery.

12
00:00:52,475 --> 00:00:59,075
The distribution of some of these is shown in Figure 66-1 (de Haan, 2018).

13
00:00:59,075 --> 00:01:07,750
In another report from the Cancer Research Network, breast malignancies made up 25 percent and thyroid cancers, 20 percent.

14
00:01:07,750 --> 00:01:14,000
Melanoma and hematological and cervical cancers each contributed approximately 10 percent .

15
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,675
Figure 66-1.

16
00:01:16,675 --> 00:01:25,800
Distribution of cancer in 1170 pregnant women form the International Network on Cancer, Infertility, and Pregnancy (INCIP).

17
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:33,762
During pregnancy, cancer management poses unique problems related to fetal concerns, and treatment is individualized.

18
00:01:33,762 --> 00:01:44,862
Considerations include the type and stage of malignancy, the desire for pregnancy continuation, and inherent risks associated with modifying or delaying cancer treatment.

19
00:01:44,862 --> 00:01:54,250
Last, adverse pregnancy outcomes have been associated in general with gravidas with cancer (Ma, 2020; Momen, 2018).

20
00:01:54,250 --> 00:01:56,887
Cancer Therapy In Pregnancy.

21
00:01:56,887 --> 00:01:59,037
# Surgery.

22
00:01:59,037 --> 00:02:05,200
Operative procedures may be indicated to aid cancer diagnosis, staging, or therapy.

23
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:13,075
Fortunately, most surgeries that do not interfere with the reproductive tract are well tolerated by both mother and fetus .

24
00:02:13,075 --> 00:02:23,075
Although many operations have classically been deferred until after 12 to 14 weeks’ gestation to minimize miscarriage risks, this probably is unnecessary.

25
00:02:23,075 --> 00:02:29,300
We believe that surgery should be performed at any gestational age if maternal well-being is imperiled.

26
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:35,375
Both pregnancy and malignancy are risk factors for venous thromboembolism (VTE).

27
00:02:35,375 --> 00:02:48,725
From studies of women with cancer during pregnancy, the risk of VTE is higher in pregnancy and in the postpartum period than in gravidas without a malignancy (Bleu, 2016; Greiber, 2021).

28
00:02:48,725 --> 00:02:55,137
Current guidelines lack specific recommendations for pregnant women undergoing surgeries for cancer.

29
00:02:55,137 --> 00:03:07,150
Thus, depending on the complexity of the planned procedure, it seems reasonable to consider prophylactic lowmolecular-weight heparin combined with elastic stockings and/or intermittent pneumatic compression .

30
00:03:07,150 --> 00:03:09,925
# Diagnostic Imaging.

31
00:03:09,925 --> 00:03:13,912
Sonography is a preferred imaging tool during pregnancy.

32
00:03:13,912 --> 00:03:28,500
Even so, the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (2019c) notes that most diagnostic radiographic procedures deliver very low x-ray doses and should not be delayed if they would directly affect therapy .

33
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:38,287
Magnetic resonance (MR) imaging can safely be performed in any trimester, but delay until after the first trimester may lower potential risks.

34
00:03:38,287 --> 00:03:52,225
Gadolinium should not be used in the first trimester and should be used later in pregnancy only when the benefits overwhelmingly outweigh risks (American College of Radiology, 2021; Kanal, 2013).

35
00:03:52,225 --> 00:04:03,525
Computed tomography (CT) is less often selected due to ionizing radiation, and procedure-related doses are listed in Chapter 49 (p. 874).

36
00:04:03,525 --> 00:04:15,375
Thus, CT imaging is used in pregnancy most often to evaluate acute concerns that include pulmonary embolism, bowel or renal obstruction, and acute neurological events.

37
00:04:15,375 --> 00:04:20,625
To enhance CT imaging, oral and intravenous contrasts may be added.

38
00:04:20,625 --> 00:04:26,112
These lack known fetal harm, and postpartum breastfeeding need not be interrupted.

39
00:04:26,112 --> 00:04:33,975
In pregnancy, some radioisotopes are relatively safe (Table 49-10, p. 876).

40
00:04:33,975 --> 00:04:36,725
# Radiation Therapy.

41
00:04:36,725 --> 00:04:44,100
Therapeutic radiation is used to treat cancers and delivers a higher radiation dose than that with diagnostic imaging.

42
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:52,675
Radiotherapy may significantly expose the fetus depending on the dose, tumor location, field size, and gestational age.

43
00:04:52,675 --> 00:05:00,212
Potential adverse effects include fetal malformation, intellectual disability, growth restriction, sterility,

44
00:05:00,364 --> 00:05:06,501
and carcinogenesis (Brent, 1999; Stovall, 1995).

45
00:05:06,451 --> 00:05:13,801
In the 2 weeks following fertilization, exposure typically leads to chromosomal damage and embryonic death.

46
00:05:13,801 --> 00:05:21,751
The next most susceptible period is during organogenesis in weeks 2 through 8, and exposure can create malformations.

47
00:05:21,751 --> 00:05:27,314
These might develop above a threshold dose of 0.1 to 0.2 Gy.

48
00:05:27,314 --> 00:05:33,251
During weeks 8 through 25, the fetal central nervous system is especially vulnerable.

49
00:05:33,251 --> 00:05:49,751
The threshold dose for intellectual disability at 8 to 15 weeks’ gestation approximates 0.06 Gy, and at 16 to 25 weeks it is about 0.25 Gy (Kal, 2005; Otake, 1996).

50
00:05:49,751 --> 00:05:59,164
After 25 weeks’ gestation, susceptibility is less, although no gestational age is considered safe for therapeutic radiation exposure.

51
00:05:59,164 --> 00:06:03,951
Thus, radiotherapy to the maternal abdomen is contraindicated.

52
00:06:03,951 --> 00:06:13,664
With some head and neck cancers, however, radiotherapy to supradiaphragmatic areas can be used relatively safely with abdominal shielding of the fetus .

53
00:06:13,664 --> 00:06:16,126
# Chemotherapy.

54
00:06:16,126 --> 00:06:21,889
Various antineoplastic drugs may be given as primary or adjunctive therapy.

55
00:06:21,889 --> 00:06:29,439
Although chemotherapy often improves long-term maternal outcomes, many are reluctant to employ it during pregnancy.

56
00:06:29,439 --> 00:06:38,451
Concerns for the fetus include malformations, growth restriction, intellectual disability, and the risk of future childhood malignancies.

57
00:06:38,451 --> 00:06:47,726
Risks depend primarily on fetal age at exposure, and most agents are potentially detrimental in the first trimester during organogenesis.

58
00:06:47,726 --> 00:06:56,614
Indeed, in one review, 14 percent of major malformations were attributable to first-trimester exposure to cytotoxic drugs .

59
00:06:56,614 --> 00:07:07,551
After the first trimester, most antineoplastic drugs are without immediate obvious adverse fetal sequelae (Korenaga, 2020; Vercruysse, 2016).

60
00:07:07,551 --> 00:07:15,414
Similarly, late mutagenic effects appear limited (Amant, 2015b; Cardonick, 2015).

61
00:07:15,414 --> 00:07:28,414
Although not always practicable, some recommend that chemotherapy be withheld in the 3 weeks before expected delivery because neutropenia or pancytopenia might cause undue risk for maternal infection or hemorrhage.

62
00:07:28,414 --> 00:07:34,901
Another concern is that neonatal hepatic and renal clearance of chemotherapy metabolites is limited .

63
00:07:34,901 --> 00:07:41,439
For these reasons, most cytotoxic chemotherapy agents are contraindicated with breastfeeding .

64
00:07:41,439 --> 00:07:44,139
# Molecular Therapy.

65
00:07:44,139 --> 00:07:50,614
Biological agents designed to stimulate hemopoiesis are commonly used with cancer treatments.

66
00:07:50,614 --> 00:07:58,776
Some of these include the granulocyte colony-stimulating factors filgrastim (Neupogen) and pegfilgrastim (Neulasta).

67
00:07:58,776 --> 00:08:04,014
If required in pregnancy, limited data support the safety of these agents .

68
00:08:04,014 --> 00:08:12,689
Red blood cells can be stimulated by erythropoietin alfa (Procrit), which from case reports also appears safe in pregnancy .

69
00:08:12,689 --> 00:08:17,026
However, maternal hypertension is a known potential risk.

70
00:08:17,026 --> 00:08:30,214
Last, for chemotherapyinduced thrombocytopenia, romiplostim and eltrombopag are thrombopoietin-receptor agonists that appear to be safe in pregnancy (Chua, 2020; Michel, 2020).

71
00:08:30,214 --> 00:08:32,826
# Targeted Therapy.

72
00:08:32,826 --> 00:08:39,251
The two main types of targeted therapy are monoclonal antibodies and smallmolecule inhibitors.

73
00:08:39,251 --> 00:08:46,526
Both block the actions of specific enzymes, proteins, or other molecules involved in cancer cell growth .

74
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:52,464
Another is nanotherapy using drugs incorporated into encapsulated nanoparticles .

75
00:08:52,464 --> 00:09:00,751
These drugs are designed to treat an ever-expanding list of cancers, and some are described in later discussions of specific tumors.

76
00:09:00,751 --> 00:09:10,214
Most of these compounds are labeled by the Food and Drug Administration as class D, and data are limited regarding their pregnancy or breastfeeding effects.

77
00:09:10,214 --> 00:09:20,864
Many of these drugs target tyrosine kinase, an important enzyme that regulates signaling pathways involved with cell division, differentiation, and apoptosis.

78
00:09:20,864 --> 00:09:27,439
With first-trimester use, embryo toxicity or teratogenicity has been attributed to these.

79
00:09:27,439 --> 00:09:32,626
Thus, use balances potential maternal benefit and potential fetal risk .

80
00:09:32,626 --> 00:09:44,401
Of other agents, the monoclonal antibody trastuzumab (Herceptin) inhibits the human epidermal growth factor receptor type 2 (HER2), which some breast cancers express.

81
00:09:44,401 --> 00:09:54,589
Although not teratogenic, its use in the second and third trimesters is associated with oligohydramnios, which appears to be reversible upon stopping the drug

82
00:09:54,748 --> 00:09:59,710
McCormick, 2018; Zagouri, 2013b).

83
00:09:59,660 --> 00:10:05,635
Because of sparse available data, other HER2 inhibitors are best avoided in pregnancy .

84
00:10:05,635 --> 00:10:09,748
# Fertility and Pregnancy after Cancer Therapy.

85
00:10:09,748 --> 00:10:16,235
Oncofertility is an emerging discipline to preserve fertility in young adults diagnosed with cancer .

86
00:10:16,235 --> 00:10:21,073
Fertility may be diminished after chemotherapy or radiotherapy.

87
00:10:21,073 --> 00:10:37,635
Counseling ideally takes place before cancer treatment, and guidelines have been developed by the American Society for Reproductive Medicine (ASRM) (2018) and other major groups (Oktay, 2018; van de Kooi, 2021).

88
00:10:37,635 --> 00:10:43,510
Prior to therapy, embryo or oocyte cryopreservation is a recognized option.

89
00:10:43,510 --> 00:10:54,248
Ovarian tissue cryopreservation is available in research settings (American Society for Reproductive Medicine, 2013a,b, 2014).

90
00:10:54,248 --> 00:11:03,698
In addition, many cancer survivors conceive by assisted reproductive technologies (ART), which by itself has associated obstetrical risks .

91
00:11:03,698 --> 00:11:12,035
If pelvic radiation is planned, surgical transposition moves ovaries and their intact primary blood supply out of the pelvis.

92
00:11:12,035 --> 00:11:19,660
The ovary is then fixed to the lateral abdominal wall at a site 3 to 4 cm above the level of the umbilicus.

93
00:11:19,660 --> 00:11:24,360
Metal clips are placed to help identify the ovary in future imaging .

94
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:32,435
In one review, functional preservation was reported in 65 to 94 percent, depending on radiotherapy type .

95
00:11:32,435 --> 00:11:49,935
In counseling cancer survivors, evidence suggests that exposure to most radiotherapy or chemotherapy agents does not significantly raise the risk of congenital anomalies or genetic disease in their offspring (Signorello, 2012; Winther, 2012).

96
00:11:49,935 --> 00:12:00,760
In those treated as children, chemotherapy does not show a consistent link to adverse obstetrical outcomes (Melin, 2015; Reulen, 2009).

97
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:14,085
Data are limited in those with cancer treated as an adult, and some studies show slightly higher rates of preterm birth and cesarean delivery (Haggar, 2014; Stensheim, 2013).

98
00:12:14,085 --> 00:12:30,048
Prior abdominopelvic radiation more convincingly affects neonatal outcomes, including elevated rates of abortion, low birthweight, stillbirth, and preterm birth (Signorello, 2006, 2010; Winther, 2008).

99
00:12:30,048 --> 00:12:40,498
Radiation may reduce uterine volume, thin the endometrium, and impair uterine blood flow (Critchley, 1992; van de Loo, 2019).

100
00:12:40,498 --> 00:12:46,273
Radiotherapy directed to the uterus and given at a younger age shows greater effects .

101
00:12:46,273 --> 00:12:49,185
# Placental Metastases.

102
00:12:49,185 --> 00:12:52,998
Tumors infrequently metastasize to the placenta.

103
00:12:52,998 --> 00:12:59,373
The most common types are malignant melanomas, leukemias, lymphomas, and breast cancer .

104
00:12:59,373 --> 00:13:05,535
Placentas from pregnancies in all women with cancer should be sent for histological evaluation.

105
00:13:05,535 --> 00:13:15,748
Tumor cells are usually confined within the intervillous spaces, and fetal metastases are rare (Al-Adnani, 2007; Rubrecht, 2020).

106
00:13:15,748 --> 00:13:18,648
Reproductive Tract Neoplasms.

107
00:13:18,648 --> 00:13:27,173
Benign neoplasms of the reproductive tract are common and include leiomyomas, ovarian tumors, and endocervical polyps.

108
00:13:27,173 --> 00:13:36,098
Cancer in these organs may also complicate pregnancy, and of these, cervical neoplasia makes up most (de Haan, 2018).

109
00:13:36,098 --> 00:13:38,235
# Cervix.

110
00:13:38,235 --> 00:13:44,085
Endocervical Polyp These are overgrowths of endocervical stroma covered by epithelium.

111
00:13:44,085 --> 00:13:52,448
They typically appear as single, red, elongated fleshy masses of variable size that extend outward from the endocervical canal.

112
00:13:52,448 --> 00:14:01,848
Usually benign, they can bleed and can be a source of Pap test results reported as atypical glandular cells of undetermined significance—AGUS.

113
00:14:01,848 --> 00:14:12,810
With removal and histological polyp evaluation, dysplasia is diagnosed in up to 0.5 percent, and cancer is found in approximately 0.1 percent .

114
00:14:12,810 --> 00:14:16,348
Few formal data guide management in pregnancy.

115
00:14:16,348 --> 00:14:22,498
Small asymptomatic lesions may be left alone to slough during delivery or puerperal remodeling.

116
00:14:22,498 --> 00:14:29,485
Removal and histological evaluation is reasonable if malignancy is suspected or if bleeding is troublesome.

117
00:14:29,485 --> 00:14:36,923
For most, the polyp is grasped with ring forceps and twisted repeatedly about its base to strangulate feeding vessels.

118
00:14:36,923 --> 00:14:40,948
With repeated twisting, the base narrows and avulses.

119
00:14:40,948 --> 00:14:47,873
Monsel paste, which is ferric subsulfate, can be applied with pressure to the stalk stub for hemostasis.

120
00:14:47,873 --> 00:14:53,060
A thick-pedicle polyp may infrequently warrant surgical ligation and excision.

121
00:14:53,060 --> 00:14:56,398
Cervical Neoplasia Pregnancy provides an

122
00:14:56,548 --> 00:15:04,010
opportune time to screen for cervical intraepithelial neoplasia (CIN) and invasive cervical cancer.

123
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:14,598
With Pap test screening, pregnancy status should be noted on the requisition form as cytological interpretation may be influenced by normal pregnancy-associated changes.

124
00:15:14,598 --> 00:15:20,773
Presence of decidual cells and, less often, an Arias-Stella reaction are examples.

125
00:15:20,773 --> 00:15:29,898
The latter gives an appearance of endocervical gland hyperplasia, which can make differentiating this from truly atypical glandular cells difficult.

126
00:15:29,898 --> 00:15:43,523
Current screening guidelines apply to both nonpregnant women and gravidas (American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists, 2021b; U.S. Preventive Services Task Force, 2018).

127
00:15:43,523 --> 00:16:01,123
Recommendations for average-risk women include: (1) no screening until age 21, (2) cytology alone every 3 years in those aged 21 to 29 years, and (3) in women aged ≥30 years, three options are suitable.

128
00:16:01,123 --> 00:16:13,548
These are human papillomavirus (HPV) plus cytology, termed co-testing, every 5 years; primary HPV testing every 5 years; or cytology every 3 years.

129
00:16:13,548 --> 00:16:27,160
Higher-risk women with altered immune systems include women with human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection, systemic lupus erythematosus, organ transplant, or immunosuppressant medication use .

130
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:35,948
Others include those with past CIN or prior early cervical cancer or in utero diethylstilbestrol (DES) exposure.

131
00:16:35,948 --> 00:16:42,973
Affected women are screened earlier and more often using current guidelines for HIV-affected individuals .

132
00:16:42,973 --> 00:16:53,385
Germane to gravidas aged ≤30 years, these guidelines recommend Pap test screening at the time of initial HIV diagnosis and then yearly.

133
00:16:53,385 --> 00:16:59,810
Once three consecutive Pap test findings are normal, screening may be spaced to every 3 years.

134
00:16:59,810 --> 00:17:02,510
Co-testing is not recommended.

135
00:17:02,510 --> 00:17:07,623
For those aged >30 years, similar Pap testing is applied.

136
00:17:07,623 --> 00:17:13,898
Co-testing is suitable for this group, and if negative, the next test can repeated in 3 years.

137
00:17:13,898 --> 00:17:16,323
Human Papillomavirus.

138
00:17:16,323 --> 00:17:19,798
This virus infects cervical epithelia.

139
00:17:19,798 --> 00:17:28,073
The infection usually clears, but in some, the virus may promote benign, premalignant, or cancerous neoplastic growth.

140
00:17:28,073 --> 00:17:37,310
The prevalence of HPV infection in pregnant women approximates 15 percent (Hong, 2013; Liu, 2014).

141
00:17:37,310 --> 00:17:47,048
Of the many HPV serotypes, several are associated with high-grade squamous intraepithelial (HSIL) lesions and invasive cancer.

142
00:17:47,048 --> 00:17:50,623
Serotypes 16 and 18 are preeminent.

143
00:17:50,623 --> 00:18:01,298
HPV testing targets only high-risk types associated with cervical neoplasia, and identification of types 16 or 18 prompts colposcopic evaluation.

144
00:18:01,298 --> 00:18:05,385
There is no indication for low-risk HPV testing.

145
00:18:05,385 --> 00:18:11,023
Serotypes HPV 6 and 11 are linked with benign maternal genital warts.

146
00:18:11,023 --> 00:18:21,348
Congenital HPV infection resulting from vertical transmission, which is mother to fetus/newborn passage, beyond transient skin colonization is rare.

147
00:18:21,348 --> 00:18:35,323
Still, conjunctival, laryngeal, vulvar, or perianal warts present at birth in the neonate or that develop within 1 to 3 years of birth are most likely due to perinatal exposure to these maternal HPV serotypes .

148
00:18:35,323 --> 00:18:42,085
Importantly, cesarean delivery does not lower the risk of neonatal laryngeal papillomatosis.

149
00:18:42,085 --> 00:18:50,723
The clear link between HPV infection and cervical neoplasia led to development of approved vaccines that reduce cervical cancer risk .

150
00:18:50,723 --> 00:18:55,073
Only one vaccine is currently available in the United States.

151
00:18:55,073 --> 00:19:09,235
Gardasil 9 is a nonavalent HPV vaccine (9vHPV) against HPV types 6, 11, 16, 18, 31, 35, 45, 52, and 58.

152
00:19:09,235 --> 00:19:14,748
This vaccine is not administered during pregnancy and is compatible with breastfeeding .

153
00:19:14,748 --> 00:19:17,910
Abnormal Cytology and Histology.

154
00:19:17,910 --> 00:19:25,948
The incidence of abnormal cervical cancer screening test results and their management is similar for gravidas and nonpregnant women.

155
00:19:25,948 --> 00:19:40,285
Current 2019 management consensus guidelines from the American Society of Colposcopy and Cervical Pathology focus on the individual’s risk for CIN 3 or cervical cancer, rather than on specific screening results .

156
00:19:40,285 --> 00:19:45,473
Management has become complex and derives from large database analyses.

157
00:19:45,473 --> 00:19:52,498
Factors include the abnormal cytology and HPV results, age, and previous screening results.

158
00:19:52,498 --> 00:19:59,373
As a result, algorithms now calculate the best clinical approach to abnormal screening test results

159
00:19:59,524 --> 00:20:05,586
www.asccp.org/management-guidelines).

160
00:20:05,536 --> 00:20:16,424
In overview, certain cytological abnormalities and HPV test results warrant colposcopy, and the main goal during pregnancy is to exclude invasive cancer.

161
00:20:16,424 --> 00:20:21,874
Thus, lesions suspicious for high-grade disease or cancer are biopsied.

162
00:20:21,874 --> 00:20:29,749
Endocervical sampling, endometrial biopsy, and treatment of preinvasive lesions are unacceptable during pregnancy.

163
00:20:29,749 --> 00:20:36,549
Women with histologically confirmed CIN from biopsy during pregnancy are allowed to deliver vaginally.

164
00:20:36,549 --> 00:20:40,924
Further evaluation is planned at least 4 weeks postpartum.

165
00:20:40,924 --> 00:20:52,549
Alternatively, for clinical findings with higher cancer risk, repeat colposcopy and cytology/HPV testing are performed at intervals no more frequently than 12 weeks.

166
00:20:52,549 --> 00:20:58,299
Biopsy is repeated only if a lesion appears worse or invasive cancer is suspected .

167
00:20:58,299 --> 00:21:06,699
Postpartum reassessment may reveal lesions missed previously due to either cervical changes of pregnancy or advancing lesion severity.

168
00:21:06,699 --> 00:21:11,999
Instead, CIN regression is common during pregnancy or puerperium.

169
00:21:11,999 --> 00:21:24,199
In one study of 1079 pregnant women with cervical dysplasia in which biopsy correlated with colposcopic findings, 61 percent of lesions reverted to normal postpartum .

170
00:21:24,199 --> 00:21:30,824
In another study, lesions regressed postpartum in 70 percent of women with CIN 2 or 3.

171
00:21:30,824 --> 00:21:38,899
However, 7 percent of CIN 2 lesions progressed to CIN 3, but no lesion advanced to invasive cancer .

172
00:21:38,899 --> 00:21:55,911
In another study of 77 women with carcinoma in situ (CIS) diagnosed antepartum, a third had postpartum regression of their lesion, two thirds had persistent CIS, and only two women had microinvasive cancer on cone biopsy after delivery .

173
00:21:55,911 --> 00:22:02,386
Adenocarcinoma in situ (AIS) is managed in a manner similar to CIN 3 .

174
00:22:02,386 --> 00:22:10,274
Thus, unless invasive cancer is identified, treatment of AIS is not recommended until 6 weeks postpartum.

175
00:22:10,274 --> 00:22:15,599
Referral to a gynecologist with advanced colposcopic skills is recommended .

176
00:22:15,599 --> 00:22:17,886
Cervical Conization.

177
00:22:17,886 --> 00:22:29,324
If invasive epithelial lesions are suspected, conization is indicated and may be done with loop electrosurgical excisional procedure (LEEP) or by cold-knife conization.

178
00:22:29,324 --> 00:22:38,399
However, the epithelium and underlying stroma within the endocervical canal cannot be extensively excised without the risk of membrane rupture.

179
00:22:38,399 --> 00:22:41,661
Logically, residual disease is common.

180
00:22:41,661 --> 00:22:50,849
Of 376 cone biopsies during pregnancy, residual neoplasia was later found in 43 percent of subsequent specimens .

181
00:22:50,849 --> 00:22:58,436
In another series, nearly 10 percent of 180 pregnant women required transfusion after conization .

182
00:22:58,436 --> 00:23:08,286
Thus, if possible, conization is avoided in pregnancy because of its higher risks for abortion, membrane rupture, hemorrhage, and preterm delivery.

183
00:23:08,286 --> 00:23:14,199
Women with CIN treated before pregnancy may also encounter pregnancy complications.

184
00:23:14,199 --> 00:23:21,474
First, distal cervical stenosis is uncommon but may follow conization, LEEP, or laser surgery.

185
00:23:21,474 --> 00:23:25,561
Cervical stenosis almost always yields during labor.

186
00:23:25,561 --> 00:23:32,236
A so-called conglutinated cervix may undergo almost complete intrapartum effacement without dilation.

187
00:23:32,236 --> 00:23:41,799
Spontaneous dilation usually promptly follows firm pressure with a fingertip, although instrumented dilation or cruciate incisions may be required.

188
00:23:41,799 --> 00:23:49,261
Second, preconceptional cold-knife conization is associated with cervical insufficiency and preterm birth.

189
00:23:49,261 --> 00:24:01,361
However, the relationship between preterm birth and LEEP continues to be debated (Castanon, 2012; Conner, 2014; Stout, 2015).

190
00:24:01,361 --> 00:24:06,661
The size of tissue excised seems to be directly related to adverse outcomes .

191
00:24:06,661 --> 00:24:17,811
Invasive Cervical Cancer This cancer is found in approximately 1 in 1200 to 10,000 pregnancies (Bigelow, 2017; McCormick, 2018).

192
00:24:17,811 --> 00:24:25,799
The diagnosis is confirmed with biopsies taken during colposcopy, with conization, or from a grossly abnormal lesion.

193
00:24:25,799 --> 00:24:34,674
Of the histological types, squamous cell carcinomas account for 75 percent, whereas adenocarcinomas compose the remainder .

194
00:24:34,674 --> 00:24:44,949
Cancers may appear as exophytic or endophytic growth; as a polyp, papillary tissue, or barrel-shaped cervix; or as focal ulceration or necrosis.

195
00:24:44,949 --> 00:24:50,061
A watery, purulent, foul, or bloody discharge may be present.

196
00:24:50,061 --> 00:24:53,674
The sensitivity of a single Pap test is poor.

197
00:24:53,674 --> 00:24:58,861
Thus, biopsy with Tischler forceps is warranted for suspicious lesions.

198
00:24:58,861 --> 00:25:01,449
Abnormal tumor vessels may

199
00:25:01,612 --> 00:25:08,462
cause heavier than expected biopsy-site bleeding, which is usually controlled by Monsel paste and pressure.

200
00:25:08,412 --> 00:25:12,849
Historically, cervical cancer was solely staged clinically.

201
00:25:12,849 --> 00:25:18,649
The current staging system now incorporates radiological and surgical evaluation .

202
00:25:18,649 --> 00:25:22,974
Lymph node metastasis is now also included in staging.

203
00:25:22,974 --> 00:25:38,037
Allowable components of clinical staging are cold-knife conization, pelvic examination under anesthesia, cystoscopy, intravenous pyelogram (or this portion of MR imaging can be used), proctoscopy, and chest radiography.

204
00:25:38,037 --> 00:25:47,462
Notably, physiological pregnancy changes may limit physical assessment of cancer extent, which is more likely to be underestimated in gravidas.

205
00:25:47,462 --> 00:26:00,299
Specifically, induration of the broad ligament base, which characterizes tumor spread beyond the cervix, may be less prominent due to cervical, paracervical, and parametrial pregnancy-induced softening.

206
00:26:00,299 --> 00:26:09,162
MR imaging can be used without gadolinium contrast to ascertain involvement of the urinary tract, parametrium, and lymph nodes .

207
00:26:09,162 --> 00:26:11,824
Management and Prognosis.

208
00:26:11,824 --> 00:26:22,462
Cervical cancer treatment in pregnant women is individualized, and factors include the clinical stage, fetal age, and individual desire to continue pregnancy.

209
00:26:22,462 --> 00:26:30,274
Stage IA1 is termed microinvasive disease and describes lesions with deepest invasion <3 mm .

210
00:26:30,274 --> 00:26:37,387
If diagnosed by cone biopsy, treatment follows guidelines similar to those for intraepithelial disease.

211
00:26:37,387 --> 00:26:46,787
In general, continuation of pregnancy and vaginal delivery are considered safe, and definitive therapy is reserved until 6 weeks postpartum.

212
00:26:46,787 --> 00:26:52,424
In contrast, cancer with greater invasion demands relatively prompt therapy.

213
00:26:52,424 --> 00:27:00,649
During the first half of pregnancy, immediate treatment is advised by most, but the decision whether to continue pregnancy is a factor.

214
00:27:00,649 --> 00:27:06,887
During the latter half of pregnancy, the risk of early delivery versus delayed treatment are weighed .

215
00:27:06,887 --> 00:27:23,012
In two studies with a total of 40 women past 20 weeks’ gestation with either stage I or stage IIA carcinoma, delayed treatment was considered reasonable in women without bulky lesions (Takushi, 2002; van Vliet, 1998).

216
00:27:23,012 --> 00:27:34,699
Another option is to complete staging using laparoscopic lymphadenectomy and to delay treatment if metastases are excluded (Alouini, 2008; Favero, 2010).

217
00:27:34,699 --> 00:27:43,474
In a metaanalysis, preoperative neoadjuvant chemotherapy with platinum derivatives was found to be promising for treatment in pregnancy .

218
00:27:43,474 --> 00:27:58,062
Although surgical therapy and radiation are equally effective, radical hysterectomy plus pelvic lymphadenectomy is the preferred treatment for invasive cervical cancer in most young women with stage I and early stage IIA lesions.

219
00:27:58,062 --> 00:28:08,824
Disadvantageously, radiotherapy for cervical cancer destroys ovarian and possibly sexual function and frequently causes intestinal and urinary tract injury.

220
00:28:08,824 --> 00:28:20,924
In 49 women with pregnancy-associated stage IB cancer, a 30-percent severe complication rate accompanied radiotherapy compared with that of only 7 percent with radical surgery .

221
00:28:20,924 --> 00:28:28,199
With surgery before 20 weeks’ gestation, radical hysterectomy is usually performed with the fetus in situ.

222
00:28:28,199 --> 00:28:34,212
In later pregnancy, however, hysterotomy and delivery is often performed first .

223
00:28:34,212 --> 00:28:36,812
Figure 66-2.

224
00:28:36,812 --> 00:28:42,274
Radical hysterectomy specimen with invasive cervical squamous cell carcinoma.

225
00:28:42,274 --> 00:28:50,849
With radical hysterectomy, the parametrium and 2 to 3 cm of vagina are excised to help achieve a tumor-free resection.

226
00:28:50,849 --> 00:28:55,274
Reproduced with permission from Dr. Debra L. Richardson.

227
00:28:55,274 --> 00:29:08,087
Although rarely selected during pregnancy, Ungár and colleagues (2006) performed abdominal radical trachelectomy before 20 weeks’ gestation for stage IB1 cancer in five pregnant women.

228
00:29:08,087 --> 00:29:19,637
One cases series describes four women with stage IA1 adenocarcinoma at 16 to 23 weeks’ gestation treated with laser conization, and all delivered at term .

229
00:29:19,637 --> 00:29:23,874
For more advanced-stage cancer, radiotherapy is given.

230
00:29:23,874 --> 00:29:29,824
External beam radiation in early in pregnancy typically leads to spontaneous abortion.

231
00:29:29,824 --> 00:29:34,174
If miscarriage does not ensue, curettage is performed.

232
00:29:34,174 --> 00:29:42,949
During the second trimester, spontaneous abortion may not promptly occur and may necessitate hysterotomy in up to a fourth of cases.

233
00:29:42,949 --> 00:29:45,587
This is selected because labor

234
00:29:45,748 --> 00:29:51,723
induction or dilation and evacuation may pose serious hemorrhage risks from the cancer.

235
00:29:51,673 --> 00:30:04,160
Pregnancy does not negatively affect cervical cancer prognosis, and survival outcomes are similar for pregnant and nonpregnant women (Amant, 2014; Mogos, 2013).

236
00:30:04,160 --> 00:30:17,335
For both of these groups, the overall 5-year survival rate approximated 80 percent in a case-control study of 44 women with pregnancy-associated cervical cancer (van der Vange, 1995).

237
00:30:17,335 --> 00:30:23,648
Delivery Adverse prognostic effects from vaginal delivery through a cancerous cervix are unknown.

238
00:30:23,648 --> 00:30:30,410
For this reason, the mode of delivery is controversial, especially for small, early-stage lesions.

239
00:30:30,410 --> 00:30:37,273
In some cases of bulky or friable tumors, hemorrhage from the cancer may complicate vaginal delivery.

240
00:30:37,273 --> 00:30:41,785
Also, recurrences in the episiotomy scar have been reported .

241
00:30:41,785 --> 00:30:45,123
Thus, most favor cesarean delivery.

242
00:30:45,123 --> 00:30:55,560
Pregnancy after Radical Trachelectomy Radical trachelectomy for stage IB1 and IB2 cervical cancer before conception is one fertility-sparing option.

243
00:30:55,560 --> 00:31:06,910
During the typically vaginal procedure, the cervix is amputated at the level of the internal os, and a permanent-suture cerclage is placed around the isthmus to support future pregnancies.

244
00:31:06,910 --> 00:31:10,748
The uterine isthmus is then reconstructed to the vagina.

245
00:31:10,748 --> 00:31:16,335
Following this, women continue to menstruate, and conception can occur naturally.

246
00:31:16,335 --> 00:31:22,348
Because of the permanent cerclage, a classical cesarean incision is required for delivery.

247
00:31:22,348 --> 00:31:31,860
Evidence suggests that cervical length <13 mm at 20 weeks’ gestation is associated with preterm birth <34 weeks .

248
00:31:31,860 --> 00:31:43,698
In a systematic review of 2566 women after radical trachelectomy for earlystage cancer, the 5-year overall maternal survival rate was 97 percent .

249
00:31:43,698 --> 00:31:49,385
The pregnancy rate was 24 percent, and the live-birth rate was 75 percent.

250
00:31:49,385 --> 00:31:51,535
# Uterus.

251
00:31:51,535 --> 00:32:00,848
Leiomyomas Also known as myomas and somewhat erroneously called fibroids, uterine leiomyomas are common benign smooth-muscle tumors.

252
00:32:00,848 --> 00:32:14,060
Their incidence during pregnancy approximates 2 percent, but the cited range depends on the frequency of routine sonography and population characteristics (Qidwai, 2006; Stout, 2010).

253
00:32:14,060 --> 00:32:24,948
In one study of 4271 women, the first-trimester myoma prevalence was highest in black women—18 percent—and lowest in whites —8 percent .

254
00:32:24,948 --> 00:32:32,323
Leiomyomas vary in location and may develop as submucosal, subserosal, or intramural growths.

255
00:32:32,323 --> 00:32:36,560
Less often, these develop in the cervix or broad ligament.

256
00:32:36,560 --> 00:32:42,273
Rare parasitic types obtain their blood supply from adjacent structures such as the omentum.

257
00:32:42,273 --> 00:32:55,285
In another rare manifestation— leiomyomatosis peritonealis disseminata—numerous, small, benign subperitoneal smooth-muscle tumors mimic carcinomatosis but often regress after pregnancy.

258
00:32:55,285 --> 00:33:01,498
In general, progesterone is considered the critical mitogen for uterine leiomyoma growth.

259
00:33:01,498 --> 00:33:07,173
In turn, estrogen functions to upregulate and maintain progesterone receptors .

260
00:33:07,173 --> 00:33:19,585
In pregnancy, progesterone’s effect on myoma growth is unpredictable, and tumor size may grow, regress, or remain unchanged (Laughlin, 2009; Neiger, 2006).

261
00:33:19,585 --> 00:33:28,110
Especially during pregnancy, these masses can be confused with other pelvic masses, and sonographic imaging is indispensable .

262
00:33:28,110 --> 00:33:36,023
Once diagnosed, myomas do not require sonographic surveillance unless associated complications are anticipated.

263
00:33:36,023 --> 00:33:43,798
With unclear sonographic findings, MR imaging may be necessary and ideally performed after the first trimester.

264
00:33:43,798 --> 00:33:46,435
Figure 66-3.

265
00:33:46,435 --> 00:33:48,823
Leiomyoma imaging.

266
00:33:48,823 --> 00:33:59,298
A. In this sagittal view from transvaginal sonography, a large uterine leiomyoma (calipers) displays heterogeneous echoes and occupies the fundus.

267
00:33:59,298 --> 00:34:06,273
This mass lies adjacent to an early first-trimester gestational sac (G) that shows a yolk sac.

268
00:34:06,273 --> 00:34:16,223
B. MR imaging at 16 weeks’ gestation shows a large leiomyoma (L) in the posterior uterine segment and cervix, which fills the pelvis.

269
00:34:16,223 --> 00:34:23,398
Associated ureteral compression and hydronephrosis required placement of a percutaneous nephrostomy tube.

270
00:34:23,398 --> 00:34:28,785
At term, planned cesarean delivery was done due to obstruction of the birth canal.

271
00:34:28,785 --> 00:34:33,573
B = bladder; F = fetus; P = placenta.

272
00:34:33,573 --> 00:34:35,310
Symptoms.

273
00:34:35,310 --> 00:34:43,548
Most leiomyomas are asymptomatic, but acute or chronic pain or pressure may develop, especially with large masses

274
00:34:43,708 --> 00:34:46,508
Doğan, 2016).

275
00:34:46,458 --> 00:34:51,483
For chronic pain, nonnarcotic analgesic drugs usually suffice.

276
00:34:51,483 --> 00:35:00,545
More acutely, some myomas can outgrow their blood supply and hemorrhagic infarction follows, which is termed red or carneous degeneration.

277
00:35:00,545 --> 00:35:08,883
Clinically, acute focal abdominal pain and tenderness are preeminent and often accompanied by leukocytosis or low-grade fever.

278
00:35:08,883 --> 00:35:15,833
Thus, tumor degeneration may be difficult to differentiate from other sources of acute abdominal pain.

279
00:35:15,833 --> 00:35:24,583
Sonography aids diagnosis, but close observation is requisite because an infarcted myoma is essentially a diagnosis of exclusion.

280
00:35:24,583 --> 00:35:29,970
Uncommonly, preterm labor is stimulated by associated inflammation.

281
00:35:29,970 --> 00:35:34,720
Symptoms from a degenerated myoma usually abate within a few days.

282
00:35:34,720 --> 00:35:40,095
In severe cases, observation may be needed to exclude a septic cause.

283
00:35:40,095 --> 00:35:47,820
Although surgery is rarely needed during pregnancy, myomectomy in highly selected cases has yielded good outcomes.

284
00:35:47,820 --> 00:36:00,533
Of 23 reported cases, women were 14 to 20 weeks’ gestation, and in almost half, surgery was performed because of pain (Celik, 2002; De Carolis, 2001).

285
00:36:00,533 --> 00:36:07,958
Except for one loss immediately following surgery at 19 weeks, most underwent cesarean delivery at term.

286
00:36:07,958 --> 00:36:15,070
Occasionally, a pedunculated subserosal myoma will undergo torsion with subsequent painful necrosis.

287
00:36:15,070 --> 00:36:21,120
Laparoscopy or laparotomy can be used to ligate the stalk and resect the necrotic tumor.

288
00:36:21,120 --> 00:36:28,433
That said, we believe that surgery should be limited to tumors with a discrete pedicle that can be easily clamped and ligated.

289
00:36:28,433 --> 00:36:30,870
Pregnancy Complications.

290
00:36:30,870 --> 00:36:43,458
Myomas have been associated with several complications that include preterm labor, placental abruption, fetal malpresentation, obstructed labor, cesarean delivery, and postpartum hemorrhage.

291
00:36:43,458 --> 00:37:00,770
In a review of pregnancy outcomes in 2065 women with myomas compared with unaffected gravidas, placental abruption and breech presentation were each increased fourfold; first-trimester bleeding and dysfunctional labor, twofold; and cesarean delivery, sixfold .

292
00:37:00,770 --> 00:37:08,883
In a report of 301 women with myomas, the preterm birth risk was 2.5-fold higher than in unaffected women .

293
00:37:08,883 --> 00:37:15,045
Another study reported an eightfold increased second-trimester abortion risk in affected women .

294
00:37:15,045 --> 00:37:28,470
Factors most important in determining morbidity in pregnancy are myoma number, size, and location (Ciavattini, 2015; Jenabi, 2018; Lam, 2014).

295
00:37:28,470 --> 00:37:39,583
If the placenta is adjacent to or implanted over a leiomyoma, the risks for abortion, preterm labor, placental abruption, and postpartum hemorrhage are all increased.

296
00:37:39,583 --> 00:37:44,658
Retroplacental myomas are also associated with fetal-growth restriction .

297
00:37:44,658 --> 00:37:52,083
Myoma-related bleeding may stem from miscarriage, preterm labor, placenta previa, and placental abruption.

298
00:37:52,083 --> 00:37:59,508
Rarely, bleeding results from a submucous myoma that has prolapsed from the uterus and into the cervix or vagina.

299
00:37:59,508 --> 00:38:10,995
In this case, although heavy or persistent bleeding may require earlier intervention, the stalk, if accessible, can be ligated vaginally near term to avoid avulsion during delivery.

300
00:38:10,995 --> 00:38:15,633
Tumors in the cervix or lower uterine segment may obstruct labor .

301
00:38:15,633 --> 00:38:28,133
Despite these complications, Qidwai and associates (2006) reported a 70-percent vaginal delivery rate even in women in whom myomas measured ≥10 cm.

302
00:38:28,133 --> 00:38:36,908
These data argue against empirical cesarean delivery, and we allow a trial of labor unless myomas clearly obstruct the birth canal.

303
00:38:36,908 --> 00:38:48,083
If cesarean delivery is indicated, uterine malrotation, which can be caused by a bulky lateral myoma, should be excluded by palpation of the fundus prior to hysterotomy .

304
00:38:48,083 --> 00:38:50,970
Myomas are generally left alone.

305
00:38:50,970 --> 00:38:58,695
Specifically, because of enucleation-associated hemorrhage, myomectomy during cesarean delivery is discouraged.

306
00:38:58,695 --> 00:39:05,395
Exceptions include recalcitrant intraoperative bleeding or a myoma that prohibits hysterotomy closure.

307
00:39:05,395 --> 00:39:13,908
With cesarean delivery in one study, mean hemoglobin levels dropped in those with myomas, but the transfusion rate was not increased .

308
00:39:13,908 --> 00:39:21,683
Importantly, cesarean hysterectomy may be technically difficult because of lateral ureteral displacement by the masses.

309
00:39:21,683 --> 00:39:24,420
Figure 66-4.

310
00:39:24,420 --> 00:39:30,433
Cesarean delivery performed because of a large leiomyoma in the lower uterine segment.

311
00:39:30,433 --> 00:39:33,020
A classical vertical uterine

312
00:39:33,172 --> 00:39:38,772
incision, seen to the left of the myoma, was required for delivery of the fetus.

313
00:39:38,722 --> 00:39:42,459
Fortunately, myomas rarely become infected .

314
00:39:42,459 --> 00:39:50,934
When infection develops, it usually is postpartum, especially if the tumor is located immediately adjacent to the implantation site .

315
00:39:50,934 --> 00:39:59,234
They also may become infected with an associated septic abortion or with myoma perforation by a sound, dilator, or curette.

316
00:39:59,234 --> 00:40:01,822
Fertility Considerations.

317
00:40:01,822 --> 00:40:08,409
Despite their relatively high prevalence in young women, their negative effect on fertility is unclear.

318
00:40:08,409 --> 00:40:17,959
Moreover, evidence from one systematic review was inconclusive to support myomectomy for intramural or subserosal myomas to improve fertility .

319
00:40:17,959 --> 00:40:31,072
As an exception, the American Society for Reproductive Medicine (2017) describes fair evidence for hysteroscopic myomectomy of submucous myomas to improve clinical pregnancy rates.

320
00:40:31,072 --> 00:40:38,847
In a systematic review of nearly 1400 pregnancies, myomas were not associated with a higher miscarriage rate .

321
00:40:38,847 --> 00:40:48,259
Instead of an infertility indication, some women may elect myomectomy to treat bleeding or pressure symptoms yet still desire fertility preservation.

322
00:40:48,259 --> 00:40:54,697
Importantly, after myomectomy, the gravid uterus can rupture either before or during labor .

323
00:40:54,697 --> 00:41:00,384
Management is individualized, and review of the prior operative report is prudent.

324
00:41:00,384 --> 00:41:09,672
If resection resulted in a defect into or immediately adjacent to the endometrial cavity, cesarean delivery is usually done before labor.

325
00:41:09,672 --> 00:41:23,484
Timing of cesarean delivery is individualized, and the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (2021b) cites between 370/7 and 386/7 weeks’ gestation.

326
00:41:23,484 --> 00:41:31,559
Uterine artery embolization of myomas is another option for women seeking symptom relief yet desiring fertility preservation .

327
00:41:31,559 --> 00:41:37,959
Women so treated have higher rates of miscarriage, cesarean delivery, and postpartum hemorrhage.

328
00:41:37,959 --> 00:41:46,897
The Society of Interventional Radiology considers myoma embolization relatively contraindicated in women who plan future pregnancies .

329
00:41:46,897 --> 00:41:51,684
Even so, myoma embolization does not harm ovarian reserve .

330
00:41:51,684 --> 00:42:03,459
Endometrial Lesions With endometriosis, studies have recently focused on a link with adverse obstetrical outcomes (Stephansson, 2009; Zullo, 2017).

331
00:42:03,459 --> 00:42:12,184
However, data are complicated by heterogeneity regarding disease stage and location, use of ART, and analysis methodologies .

332
00:42:12,184 --> 00:42:17,334
Despite this, an association with placenta previa is the most consistent.

333
00:42:17,334 --> 00:42:26,622
Occasionally, an endometrioma can develop after delivery from endometrial tissue implanted within laparotomy or episiotomy scars.

334
00:42:26,622 --> 00:42:31,559
Pfannenstiel incisions carry greater susceptibility than vertical ones .

335
00:42:31,559 --> 00:42:36,234
These form a palpable mass and can cause cyclical localized pain.

336
00:42:36,234 --> 00:42:40,709
Endometriomas within an ovary are discussed in the next section.

337
00:42:40,709 --> 00:42:45,772
Adenomyosis is traditionally found in late reproductive life and beyond.

338
00:42:45,772 --> 00:42:54,247
Its acquisition may be at least partially related to disruption of the endometrial-myometrial border during sharp curettage for abortion .

339
00:42:54,247 --> 00:43:03,872
In one systematic review, miscarriage, poor fetal growth, preeclampsia, placenta previa, and preterm delivery were associated risks .

340
00:43:03,872 --> 00:43:13,972
Endometrial carcinoma is an estrogen-dependent neoplasia also usually found in women aged >40 years and thus seen only rarely with pregnancy .

341
00:43:13,972 --> 00:43:23,847
Of 27 cases that were identified during pregnancy or within the first 4 months postpartum, most were found in first-trimester curettage specimens .

342
00:43:23,847 --> 00:43:35,484
These are usually early-stage, welldifferentiated adenocarcinomas for which treatment consists primarily of total abdominal hysterectomy and bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy.

343
00:43:35,484 --> 00:43:41,984
For nonpregnant women, surgical management of early endometrial cancer is also the standard.

344
00:43:41,984 --> 00:43:56,672
However, to preserve fertility potential in a well-counseled woman with early-stage, well-differentiated, endometrioid endometrial cancer, treatment with oral or intrauterine progestin therapy can be used to prompt tumor regression .

345
00:43:56,672 --> 00:44:02,734
Notably, live birth rates are low, and a large percentage requires ART for conception .

346
00:44:02,734 --> 00:44:06,609
Moreover, recurrences and deaths have been reported .

347
00:44:06,609 --> 00:44:08,647
# Ovary.

348
00:44:08,647 --> 00:44:12,397
Ovarian masses found during pregnancy are common.

349
00:44:12,397 --> 00:44:17,509
Incidences vary depending on the frequency of prenatal sonography, the

350
00:44:17,668 --> 00:44:23,793
ovarian size threshold, and study site designation as tertiary or primary care.

351
00:44:23,743 --> 00:44:34,868
Thus, the incidence of ovarian masses not surprisingly ranges from 1 in 100 to 2000 pregnancies (Bacalbaşa, 2020; Korenaga, 2020).

352
00:44:34,868 --> 00:44:42,693
Of ovarian malignancies, the incidence in the California Cancer Registry was 1 case in 19,000 pregnancies .

353
00:44:42,693 --> 00:44:53,468
The most frequent types of ovarian masses are corpus luteum cysts, endometriomas, benign cystadenomas, and mature cystic teratomas (dermoid cysts).

354
00:44:53,468 --> 00:45:03,243
In one series of 53 endometriomas diagnosed in the first trimester, a fourth each remained stable or increased in size, and a third shrank .

355
00:45:03,243 --> 00:45:07,893
Mature cystic teratomas enlarge infrequently during pregnancy.

356
00:45:07,893 --> 00:45:15,980
Rarely, a teratoma may express N-methyl-D-aspartate (NMDA) receptors within the tumor’s neural-tissue component.

357
00:45:15,980 --> 00:45:22,718
Antibodies form against these receptors within the tumor and then attack similar-looking receptors in the brain.

358
00:45:22,718 --> 00:45:28,043
In one case, a pregnant woman developed encephalitis from these antibodies .

359
00:45:28,043 --> 00:45:35,705
Because pregnant women are usually young, malignant tumors and those of low malignant potential are proportionately uncommon.

360
00:45:35,705 --> 00:45:45,730
One study found that 1 percent of 9375 ovarian masses were frankly malignant and that another 1 percent were of low malignant potential .

361
00:45:45,730 --> 00:45:56,068
In surgically excised masses, rates of malignancy are higher, vary from 4 to 13 percent, and probably reflect a greater preoperative concern for cancer .

362
00:45:56,068 --> 00:46:00,105
Diagnosis Most ovarian masses are asymptomatic.

363
00:46:00,105 --> 00:46:07,618
Some cause pressure or chronic pain, and acute abdominal pain may be due to torsion, rupture, or hemorrhage.

364
00:46:07,618 --> 00:46:11,755
Rarely, blood loss is sufficient to cause hypovolemia.

365
00:46:11,755 --> 00:46:21,280
Ovarian masses are usually detected during routine prenatal sonography or during imaging for other indications, including symptom evaluation.

366
00:46:21,280 --> 00:46:26,480
For complicated anatomy, MR imaging can be used without contrast.

367
00:46:26,480 --> 00:46:36,043
Cancer antigen 125 (CA125) is a tumor marker, and levels are frequently elevated with ovarian malignancy.

368
00:46:36,043 --> 00:46:45,330
Importantly, in early pregnancy and early puerperium, CA125 levels are normally elevated, possibly from the decidua.

369
00:46:45,330 --> 00:46:57,993
From the second trimester until term, levels are not normally higher than those in the nonpregnant woman (Appendix, p. 1229) (Korenaga, 2020; Szecsi, 2014).

370
00:46:57,993 --> 00:47:03,705
With severe preeclampsia, however, concentrations are abnormally elevated .

371
00:47:03,705 --> 00:47:21,855
Other tumor markers that have been used for diagnosis or posttreatment surveillance in pregnancy include human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG), alpha-fetoprotein (AFP), inhibins A and B, carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA), and the multimarker OVA1 test .

372
00:47:21,855 --> 00:47:27,618
Complications Torsion and hemorrhage are significant complications of adnexal masses.

373
00:47:27,618 --> 00:47:36,380
Torsion usually causes acute constant or episodic lower abdominal pain and tenderness that is accompanied frequently by nausea and vomiting.

374
00:47:36,380 --> 00:47:44,030
Transvaginal sonography (TVS) often aids diagnosis, and an adnexal mass is typically comorbid.

375
00:47:44,030 --> 00:47:48,668
With color Doppler, absent flow strongly correlates with torsion.

376
00:47:48,668 --> 00:47:56,243
However, minimal or early twisting may compromise only venous flow, thus leaving the arterial supply intact.

377
00:47:56,243 --> 00:48:14,205
Other sonographic signs are ovarian stromal edema; follicle displacement to the ovarian periphery; free cul-de-sac fluid; the whirlpool sign, which displays twisted vessels of the involved pedicle; and the follicular ring sign (Moro, 2020; Yatsenko, 2021).

378
00:48:14,205 --> 00:48:23,055
This last sign is a 1- to 2-mm echogenic rim around antral follicles and may reflect edema and engorged capillaries.

379
00:48:23,055 --> 00:48:28,118
If torsion is suspected, laparoscopy or laparotomy is warranted.

380
00:48:28,118 --> 00:48:33,643
Contrary to prior teaching, most now recommend untwisting to save the ovary .

381
00:48:33,643 --> 00:48:38,505
Concerns for thrombus release and pulmonary embolism have been allayed .

382
00:48:38,505 --> 00:48:41,805
A grossly necrotic adnexum is removed.

383
00:48:41,805 --> 00:48:49,493
With a salvageable ovary, within minutes of untwisting, congestion is relieved but the blue-black color typically persists.

384
00:48:49,493 --> 00:48:52,268
Figure 66-5.

385
00:48:52,268 --> 00:48:54,755
Ovarian torsion at term.

386
00:48:54,755 --> 00:49:01,005
The patient underwent cesarean delivery, and the left uteroovarian pedicle was untwisted.

387
00:49:01,005 --> 00:49:05,255
Reproduced with permission from Dr. C. Edward Wells.

388
00:49:05,255 --> 00:49:09,105
If the adnexum is deemed viable, there are options.

389
00:49:09,105 --> 00:49:12,880
First, an associated neoplasm is resected.

390
00:49:12,880 --> 00:49:16,793
However, ovarian cystectomy in an edematous

391
00:49:16,948 --> 00:49:22,110
ovary may be technically difficult, and adnexectomy may be necessary.

392
00:49:22,060 --> 00:49:30,023
Less often, cystectomy may be delayed for low-risk lesions to allow easier enucleation following edema resolution .

393
00:49:30,023 --> 00:49:36,648
Second, oophoropexy, especially for a second case of torsion, can minimize recurrence risk .

394
00:49:36,648 --> 00:49:48,810
Techniques described include shortening of the uteroovarian ligament with a running stitch or fixing the uteroovarian ligament to the posterior uterus, the lateral pelvic wall, or the round ligament .

395
00:49:48,810 --> 00:49:54,423
The most common cause of ovarian hemorrhage follows rupture of a corpus luteum cyst.

396
00:49:54,423 --> 00:50:00,260
Symptoms mirror those of hemoperitoneum, and diffuse lower abdominal pain is usual.

397
00:50:00,260 --> 00:50:08,323
TVS shows blood in the cul-de-sac and a collapsed ovarian cyst remnant (Fig. 12-5, p. 224).

398
00:50:08,323 --> 00:50:14,723
If the diagnosis is certain and symptoms abate, observation and surveillance is usually sufficient.

399
00:50:14,723 --> 00:50:19,660
Concern for ongoing bleeding will typically prompt surgical evaluation.

400
00:50:19,660 --> 00:50:27,748
If the corpus luteum is removed before 10 weeks’ gestation, progestational support is recommended to maintain the pregnancy.

401
00:50:27,748 --> 00:50:54,985
Suitable regimens include: (1) micronized progesterone (Prometrium), 200 or 300 mg orally once daily; (2) 8-percent progesterone vaginal gel (Crinone), one premeasured applicator vaginally daily, plus micronized progesterone, 100 or 200 mg orally once daily; or (3) intramuscular 17-hydroxyprogesterone caproate, 150 mg.

402
00:50:54,985 --> 00:50:59,110
The first two regimens are given until 10 completed weeks.

403
00:50:59,110 --> 00:51:07,048
For the last, if given between 8 and 10 weeks’ gestation, only one injection is required immediately after surgery.

404
00:51:07,048 --> 00:51:15,835
If the corpus luteum is excised between 6 and 8 weeks’ gestation, two additional doses should be given 1 and 2 weeks after the first.

405
00:51:15,835 --> 00:51:24,885
Asymptomatic Adnexal Mass During Pregnancy Most of these are incidentally found, and decisions include necessity and timing of resection.

406
00:51:24,885 --> 00:51:32,660
A cystic benign-appearing mass measuring <5 cm often requires no additional antepartum surveillance.

407
00:51:32,660 --> 00:51:40,148
Early in pregnancy, this is likely a corpus luteum cyst, which typically resolves by the early second trimester.

408
00:51:40,148 --> 00:51:50,385
For cysts ≥10 cm, the risk of malignancy, torsion, or labor obstruction is substantial, and surgical removal is reasonable.

409
00:51:50,385 --> 00:51:58,735
Tumors between 5 and 10 cm are carefully evaluated by TVS coupled with color Doppler and possibly MR imaging.

410
00:51:58,735 --> 00:52:10,873
Simple-appearing cysts can be managed expectantly with sonographic surveillance (American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists, 2016; Schmeler, 2005).

411
00:52:10,873 --> 00:52:16,885
Resection is done if cysts grow, display malignant qualities, or become symptomatic.

412
00:52:16,885 --> 00:52:26,848
Those with classic findings of endometrioma or mature cystic teratoma may be resected postpartum or during cesarean delivery for obstetrical indications.

413
00:52:26,848 --> 00:52:29,648
Figure 66-6.

414
00:52:29,648 --> 00:52:34,560
Sonographic characteristics of common adnexal masses in pregnancy.

415
00:52:34,560 --> 00:52:43,585
A. A simple hemorrhagic cyst with smooth walls and an internal reticular pattern is characteristic of a physiological corpus luteum cyst.

416
00:52:43,585 --> 00:52:51,998
B. Homogeneous cystic mass with diffuse internal low-level echoes suggestive of an endometrioma or hemorrhagic corpus luteum.

417
00:52:51,998 --> 00:52:58,323
C. Mature cystic teratoma (dermoid cyst) appears as a complex adnexal cyst.

418
00:52:58,323 --> 00:53:05,673
On the right side, hyperechoic lines and dots represent hair in both longitudinal and transverse planes.

419
00:53:05,673 --> 00:53:12,673
At the central superior aspect of this cyst, a mural nodule—the Rokitansky protuberance—is seen.

420
00:53:12,673 --> 00:53:19,148
A fat (right side)-fluid (left side) level is another common finding with these tumors.

421
00:53:19,148 --> 00:53:25,423
On the other hand, if sonographic findings suggest cancer, prompt resection is indicated .

422
00:53:25,423 --> 00:53:34,423
Nodules, papillary excrescences, solid components, or thick, vascular septa within the mass or ascites are suggestive findings .

423
00:53:34,423 --> 00:53:42,310
In one review of 563 masses in pregnancy, approximately half were simple, and the other half complex .

424
00:53:42,310 --> 00:53:49,198
Among simple masses, 1 percent were malignant, and of complex masses, 9 percent were cancerous.

425
00:53:49,198 --> 00:53:55,973
Approximately 1 in 1000 pregnant women undergoes surgical exploration for an adnexal mass .

426
00:53:55,973 --> 00:54:04,423
In general, we plan resection at 14 to 20 weeks’ gestation because most masses that will regress will have done so by this time.

427
00:54:04,423 --> 00:54:11,435
Laparoscopic removal is ideal (Naqvi, 2015; Sisodia, 2015).

428
00:54:11,435 --> 00:54:13,535
Importantly, the

429
00:54:13,684 --> 00:54:35,396
American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (2016) recommends consultation with a gynecological oncologist for elements implicating cancer that include a very elevated CA125 level, a nodular or fixed pelvic mass, ascites, evidence of metastasis, or ultrasound findings suggesting malignancy.

430
00:54:35,396 --> 00:54:45,309
Pregnancy-Related Ovarian Tumors One group of ovarian masses results directly from the stimulating effects of various pregnancy hormones on ovarian stroma.

431
00:54:45,309 --> 00:54:52,534
These include pregnancy luteoma, hyperreactio luteinalis, and ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome.

432
00:54:52,534 --> 00:54:54,721
Pregnancy Luteoma.

433
00:54:54,721 --> 00:55:07,084
This is a rare, benign ovarian neoplasm that arises from luteinized stromal cells and classically raises testosterone levels (Hakim, 2016; Irving, 2011).

434
00:55:07,084 --> 00:55:16,909
Up to 25 percent of affected women will be virilized, and of these affected women, nearly half of their female fetuses will have some degree of virilization.

435
00:55:16,909 --> 00:55:26,759
However, most mothers and their fetuses may be unaffected because the placenta rapidly converts testosterone to estrogen (Kaňová, 2011).

436
00:55:26,759 --> 00:55:36,859
In typical cases, an adnexal mass along with maternal virilization will prompt sonography and measurement of testosterone and CA125 levels.

437
00:55:36,859 --> 00:55:45,284
Luteomas are variably sized, appear solid, may be multiple or bilateral, and may be complex because of internal hemorrhage .

438
00:55:45,284 --> 00:55:53,896
Concerns for malignancy may be further investigated with MR imaging (Kao, 2005; Tannus, 2009).

439
00:55:53,896 --> 00:56:03,609
Total testosterone levels are increased, but notably, levels in normal pregnancy can be substantially elevated (Appendix, p. 1231).

440
00:56:03,609 --> 00:56:15,834
Differential diagnoses include granulosa cell tumors, thecomas, Sertoli-Leydig cell tumors, Leydig cell tumors, stromal hyperthecosis, and hyperreactio luteinalis.

441
00:56:15,834 --> 00:56:23,634
Generally, luteomas do not require surgical intervention unless torsion, rupture, or hemorrhage complicate these .

442
00:56:23,634 --> 00:56:31,846
Tumors spontaneously regress during the first few months postpartum, and androgen levels drop precipitously following delivery .

443
00:56:31,846 --> 00:56:35,996
Lactation may be delayed a week by hyperandrogenemia .

444
00:56:35,996 --> 00:56:39,471
Recurrence in subsequent pregnancies is rare.

445
00:56:39,471 --> 00:56:42,071
Hyperreactio Luteinalis.

446
00:56:42,071 --> 00:56:49,996
In this condition, one or both ovaries develop multiple, large theca-lutein cysts, typically after the first trimester.

447
00:56:49,996 --> 00:56:58,621
Cysts are caused by luteinization of the follicular theca interna layer, and most are stimulated by exceptionally high hCG levels .

448
00:56:58,621 --> 00:57:08,171
Thus, they are more common with gestational trophoblastic disease, twins, fetal hydrops, and other conditions with increased placental mass .

449
00:57:08,171 --> 00:57:11,884
Maternal but not fetal virilization may develop .

450
00:57:11,884 --> 00:57:16,796
Serum testosterone levels are not predictive of maternal virilization .

451
00:57:16,796 --> 00:57:24,571
Sonographically, these ovarian tumors have a “spoke wheel” pattern (Fig. 13-3, p. 238) .

452
00:57:24,571 --> 00:57:32,321
If the diagnosis is confident, and unless complicated by torsion or hemorrhage, surgical intervention is not required.

453
00:57:32,321 --> 00:57:35,296
These masses resolve after delivery.

454
00:57:35,296 --> 00:57:44,234
Few data allow prediction of recurrence in a subsequent pregnancy, but in one case report, a woman had hyperreactio with three pregnancies .

455
00:57:44,234 --> 00:57:47,284
Ovarian Hyperstimulation Syndrome.

456
00:57:47,284 --> 00:57:54,171
This is typified by multiple ovarian follicular cysts accompanied by increased capillary permeability.

457
00:57:54,171 --> 00:58:03,271
It most often is a complication of ovulation-induction therapy for infertility, although it rarely may develop in an otherwise normal pregnancy.

458
00:58:03,271 --> 00:58:13,746
Its etiopathogenesis is thought to involve hCG stimulation of vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) expression in granulosa-lutein cells .

459
00:58:13,746 --> 00:58:24,959
This causes greater vascular permeability that can lead to ascites, pleural or pericardial effusion, hypovolemia with acute kidney injury, and hypercoagulability.

460
00:58:24,959 --> 00:58:33,446
Serious complications are renal dysfunction, adult respiratory distress syndrome, ovarian rupture with hemorrhage, and VTE.

461
00:58:33,446 --> 00:58:38,021
Unlike hyperreactio lutealis, virilization is absent .

462
00:58:38,021 --> 00:58:44,571
Management is outlined by the American Society for Reproductive Medicine (2016).

463
00:58:44,571 --> 00:58:50,246
Treatment is primarily supportive to maintain vascular volume and prevent VTE.

464
00:58:50,246 --> 00:58:54,296
In severe cases, paracentesis can be helpful.

465
00:58:54,296 --> 00:59:01,346
Ovarian Cancer Malignancies of the ovary are the leading cause of death from genital-tract cancers in all women .

466
00:59:01,346 --> 00:59:05,259
Still, the incidence of ovarian malignancy only

467
00:59:05,428 --> 00:59:13,565
ranges from 1 case in 20,000 to 50,000 births (Eibye, 2013; Smith, 2003).

468
00:59:13,515 --> 00:59:22,753
Of those found in pregnancy, 75 percent are early-stage cancers that carry a 5-year survival rate between 70 and 90 percent .

469
00:59:22,753 --> 00:59:28,853
The types of malignancy are also markedly different in gravidas compared with those in older women.

470
00:59:28,853 --> 00:59:39,678
In pregnant women, these are, in decreasing order of frequency, germ cell and sex cord-stromal tumors, low-malignant-potential tumors, and epithelial cancers .

471
00:59:39,678 --> 00:59:45,153
Pregnancy apparently does not alter the prognosis of most ovarian malignancies.

472
00:59:45,153 --> 00:59:53,340
Management is similar to that for nonpregnant women, with the usual proviso that it may be modified depending on gestational age.

473
00:59:53,340 --> 01:00:06,940
Thus, if frozen-section histopathological analysis verifies malignancy, surgical staging is done with careful inspection of all accessible peritoneal and visceral surfaces (Bacalbaşa, 2020).

474
01:00:06,940 --> 01:00:21,015
Peritoneal washings are taken for cytology, biopsies are obtained from the diaphragmatic surface and peritoneum, omentectomy is completed, and pelvic and infrarenal paraaortic lymph nodes are sampled, if accessible.

475
01:00:21,015 --> 01:00:27,840
If disease is advanced, bilateral adnexectomy and omentectomy will decrease most tumor burden.

476
01:00:27,840 --> 01:00:34,353
In early pregnancy, hysterectomy and aggressive surgical debulking procedures may be elected.

477
01:00:34,353 --> 01:00:41,815
In other cases, minimal debulking described in the previous paragraph is done, and the operation is terminated.

478
01:00:41,815 --> 01:00:50,340
In some cases of aggressive or large-volume disease, chemotherapy can be given during pregnancy while awaiting pulmonary maturation.

479
01:00:50,340 --> 01:00:57,465
Monitoring maternal CA125 serum levels during chemotherapy is not accurate in pregnancy .

480
01:00:57,465 --> 01:01:05,053
Preventively, increasing parity is one known factor (Fortner, 2019; Huang, 2020).

481
01:01:05,053 --> 01:01:10,265
A metaanalysis also found that prior miscarriage or abortion lowered risk .

482
01:01:10,265 --> 01:01:23,190
Of modifiable factors, combination oral contraceptives and breastfeeding lower ovarian cancer rates (Babic, 2020; Havrilesky, 2013; Iversen, 2018).

483
01:01:23,190 --> 01:01:33,078
Discussed in Chapter 39 (p. 682), rates of some ovarian cancers may decline following tubal interruption and perhaps salpingectomy.

484
01:01:33,078 --> 01:01:35,665
# Adnexal Cysts.

485
01:01:35,665 --> 01:01:43,765
Paratubal and paraovarian cysts either are distended remnants of the paramesonephric ducts or are mesothelial inclusion cysts.

486
01:01:43,765 --> 01:01:49,215
One autopsy series in nonpregnant women cited an incidence of 5 percent .

487
01:01:49,215 --> 01:01:57,278
The most common paramesonephric cyst is the hydatid of Morgagni, which is pedunculated and typically dangles from one of the fimbria.

488
01:01:57,278 --> 01:02:06,440
Although these may undergo torsion, other complications are rare, and most are identified during cesarean delivery or puerperal sterilization.

489
01:02:06,440 --> 01:02:13,053
In these instances, they can simply be excised or drained by creating a large window in the cyst wall.

490
01:02:13,053 --> 01:02:24,390
Neoplastic paraovarian cysts are rare, sonographically and histologically resemble tumors of ovarian origin, and rarely are of borderline potential or frankly malignant .

491
01:02:24,390 --> 01:02:27,128
# Vulva and Vagina.

492
01:02:27,128 --> 01:02:41,640
Preinvasive disease in young women—vulvar intraepithelial neoplasia (VIN) and vaginal intraepithelial neoplasia (VAIN)—are seen more often than invasive disease and are commonly associated with HPV infection.

493
01:02:41,640 --> 01:02:47,415
As with cervical neoplasia, these premalignant conditions are treated after delivery.

494
01:02:47,415 --> 01:02:59,440
Cancer of the vulva or vagina is generally a malignancy of older women, and thus, these are rarely associated with pregnancy (Amant, 2019; Korenaga, 2020).

495
01:02:59,440 --> 01:03:03,365
Even so, any suspicious lesion is biopsied.

496
01:03:03,365 --> 01:03:10,790
Most are squamous cell cancers, and treatment is individualized according to the clinical stage and depth of invasion.

497
01:03:10,790 --> 01:03:21,303
In a review of 23 cases, investigators concluded that radical surgery for stage I disease was feasible during pregnancy—including in the last trimester .

498
01:03:21,303 --> 01:03:27,853
It appears that vaginal delivery is not contraindicated if vulvar and inguinal incisions are well healed.

499
01:03:27,853 --> 01:03:35,503
In late pregnancy, resection and definitive therapy can often be delayed due to these tumors’ typically slow progression .

500
01:03:35,503 --> 01:03:46,653
Other vulvar cancer types and vaginal malignancies are rare in pregnancy and mainly the subjects of case reports (Korenaga, 2020; Matsuo, 2009).

501
01:03:46,653 --> 01:03:48,740
Breast Carcinoma.

502
01:03:48,740 --> 01:03:56,290
Breast cancer incidence in women aged 25 to 40 years has been rising since the 1930s (American

503
01:03:56,452 --> 01:04:01,189
Cancer Society, 2021; Lima, 2020).

504
01:04:01,139 --> 01:04:14,939
It has an overall relatively high frequency in younger women and is the most frequent cancer complicating pregnancy (see Fig. 66-1) (Alfasi, 2019; de Hann, 2018).

505
01:04:14,939 --> 01:04:21,739
From the Nationwide Inpatient Sample, the incidence approximated 1 case in 15,000 births .

506
01:04:21,739 --> 01:04:34,014
Postponed childbearing was considered partially responsible for the increase in pregnancy-associated breast cancer in Sweden and Denmark (Andersson, 2015; Eibye, 2013).

507
01:04:34,014 --> 01:04:41,289
And, as more women choose to delay childbearing, the frequency of associated breast cancer is certain to rise.

508
01:04:41,289 --> 01:04:49,389
Genetic mutations underlie some breast cancer cases, and these are discussed in that section (p. 1174).

509
01:04:49,389 --> 01:04:51,789
# Diagnosis.

510
01:04:51,789 --> 01:05:00,164
More than 90 percent of gravidas with breast cancer have a palpable mass, and greater than 80 percent of cases are self-reported .

511
01:05:00,164 --> 01:05:08,464
In pregnancy, clinical assessment, diagnostic procedures, and treatment of women with breast tumors are often slightly delayed .

512
01:05:08,464 --> 01:05:14,414
This is partially attributed to pregnancy-induced growth of breast tissue that obscures masses.

513
01:05:14,414 --> 01:05:23,152
Breast mass evaluation does not differ from that for nonpregnant women (Loibl, 2015; McCormick, 2018).

514
01:05:23,152 --> 01:05:27,877
Thus, any suspicious breast mass should be pursued to diagnosis.

515
01:05:27,877 --> 01:05:33,052
Pragmatically, a palpable discrete mass can be biopsied or excised.

516
01:05:33,052 --> 01:05:39,764
To distinguish between a solid and cystic lesion, sonography has high sensitivity and specificity .

517
01:05:39,764 --> 01:05:49,289
Mammography is appropriate if indicated, and the fetal radiation risk is negligible—0.04 mGy—with appropriate shielding .

518
01:05:49,289 --> 01:05:57,014
But, because breast tissue is denser in pregnancy, mammography has a falsenegative rate of 35 to 40 percent .

519
01:05:57,014 --> 01:06:02,052
If the decision to biopsy is uncertain, MR imaging may be used.

520
01:06:02,052 --> 01:06:13,689
To better classify imaging findings for breast masses, the American College of Radiology (2013) developed the Breast Imaging-Reporting and Data System—BI-RADS.

521
01:06:13,689 --> 01:06:23,477
Suitable for sonography, mammographic, and MR imaging results, the intent is to communicate an individual woman’s risk of developing breast cancer .

522
01:06:23,477 --> 01:06:26,114
Table 66-1.

523
01:06:26,114 --> 01:06:36,439
American College of Radiology: Breast Imaging Reporting and Data Systems—BI-RADSa Cystic breast lesions are simple, complicated, or complex.

524
01:06:36,439 --> 01:06:43,314
Simple cysts do not require special management or monitoring, but they may be aspirated if symptomatic.

525
01:06:43,314 --> 01:06:50,989
Complicated cysts show internal echoes during sonography, and they sometimes are indistinguishable from solid masses.

526
01:06:50,989 --> 01:07:00,064
These are typically aspirated, and if the sonographic abnormality does not resolve completely, a core-needle biopsy is usually performed.

527
01:07:00,064 --> 01:07:05,177
Complex cysts have septa or intracystic masses seen sonographically.

528
01:07:05,177 --> 01:07:11,052
Because some breast cancer may form complex cysts, excision is usually recommended.

529
01:07:11,052 --> 01:07:19,939
For solid breast masses, evaluation uses the triple test, that is, clinical examination, imaging, and core needle biopsy.

530
01:07:19,939 --> 01:07:27,089
If all three suggest a benign lesion or if all three suggest a breast cancer, the test is considered concordant.

531
01:07:27,089 --> 01:07:37,327
A concordant benign triple test is ≥99-percent accurate, and breast lumps in this category can be followed by clinical examination alone.

532
01:07:37,327 --> 01:07:41,714
Most masses in pregnancy have these three reassuring features.

533
01:07:41,714 --> 01:07:47,939
In contrast, if any of the three assessments suggests malignancy, the mass should be excised.

534
01:07:47,939 --> 01:07:50,164
# Management.

535
01:07:50,164 --> 01:07:55,839
With breast cancer, a limited search of the most common metastatic sites is completed.

536
01:07:55,839 --> 01:08:06,352
For most, this includes a chest radiograph, liver sonography, and skeletal MR imaging (Becker, 2016; Krishna, 2013).

537
01:08:06,352 --> 01:08:11,439
MR imaging can also evaluate the abdomen, pelvis, and brain.

538
01:08:11,439 --> 01:08:17,802
Treatment of breast cancer includes an obstetrician, breast surgeon, and medical oncologist.

539
01:08:17,802 --> 01:08:28,514
Initially, desires for pregnancy continuation are addressed, and data indicate that pregnancy interruption does not influence the course or prognosis of breast cancer .

540
01:08:28,514 --> 01:08:34,189
With pregnancy continuation, treatment in general mirrors that for nonpregnant women.

541
01:08:34,189 --> 01:08:43,677
Important caveats are that chemotherapy and surgery are postponed to the second trimester, and adjuvant radiotherapy is withheld until after delivery .

542
01:08:43,677 --> 01:08:50,477
Delay should be avoided as the risk of metastases increases with every few months by 5 to 10 percent .

543
01:08:50,477 --> 01:08:52,577
Surgical treatment

544
01:08:52,732 --> 01:08:54,832
may be definitive.

545
01:08:54,782 --> 01:09:04,594
In the absence of metastatic disease, either a wide excision or a modified or total mastectomy—each with axillary node staging—can be performed .

546
01:09:04,594 --> 01:09:11,407
Staging by sentinel lymph node biopsy and lymphoscintigraphy with technetium-99m is safe.

547
01:09:11,407 --> 01:09:16,807
Breast reconstruction, if desired, is typically delayed until after delivery .

548
01:09:16,807 --> 01:09:24,769
That said, one small series showed good results in 10 pregnant women who underwent immediate reconstruction after mastectomy .

549
01:09:24,769 --> 01:09:30,219
Chemotherapy is usually given with both positive- and negative-node breast cancers.

550
01:09:30,219 --> 01:09:37,207
In premenopausal women, survival rates with this approach are improved, even if lymph nodes are cancer free.

551
01:09:37,207 --> 01:09:45,069
For node-positive disease, multiagent chemotherapy is begun if delivery is not anticipated within several weeks.

552
01:09:45,069 --> 01:09:50,344
Cyclophosphamide, doxorubicin, and cisplatin are currently used .

553
01:09:50,344 --> 01:10:00,532
If an anthracycline-based agent such as doxorubicin is used, pretherapy maternal echocardiography is performed because of associated cardiotoxicity .

554
01:10:00,532 --> 01:10:07,819
Good maternal and perinatal results have been reported (Freret, 2020; McCormick, 2018).

555
01:10:07,819 --> 01:10:11,857
Immunotherapy for breast cancers is now commonplace.

556
01:10:11,857 --> 01:10:21,857
Trastuzumab (Herceptin) is a monoclonal antibody to the HER2/neu receptor, which is found in approximately a third of invasive breast cancers .

557
01:10:21,857 --> 01:10:25,032
The drug is not recommended in pregnancy.

558
01:10:25,032 --> 01:10:41,844
This is because HER2/neu is strongly expressed in fetal renal epithelium, and trastuzumab has been linked with miscarriage, fetal renal failure and related oligohydramnios, and preterm birth (Amant, 2010; Azim, 2010).

559
01:10:41,844 --> 01:10:47,494
The effects of pregnancy on the course of breast cancer and its prognosis are complex.

560
01:10:47,494 --> 01:10:55,207
Breast cancer is more aggressive in younger women, but whether it is more aggressive during pregnancy in these same women is debatable .

561
01:10:55,207 --> 01:11:05,757
Clinically, most studies indicate little difference in overall survival rates with pregnancy-associated breast cancer compared with similarly aged and staged nonpregnant women .

562
01:11:05,757 --> 01:11:11,657
Other reports note worse overall survival rates with pregnancy-associated breast cancer .

563
01:11:11,657 --> 01:11:18,594
These investigators do conclude, however, that later disease stages are more prevalent in pregnant women.

564
01:11:18,594 --> 01:11:26,169
Because breast cancer is usually found at a more advanced stage in pregnant women, the overall prognosis is diminished .

565
01:11:26,169 --> 01:11:36,144
The aggregate of studies published after 1990 indicate that up to 60 percent of pregnant women have concomitant axillary node involvement at diagnosis.

566
01:11:36,144 --> 01:11:51,807
And although, stage for stage, the 5-year survival rate is comparable in pregnant and nonpregnant women, the more advanced stages that are typical of pregnant women worsen their prognosis (Kuo, 2019; Zemlickis, 1992).

567
01:11:51,807 --> 01:11:55,169
# Pregnancy Following Breast Cancer.

568
01:11:55,169 --> 01:12:04,669
After breast cancer treatment, chemotherapy will render some women infertile, but childbearing options were noted earlier (p. 1164).

569
01:12:04,669 --> 01:12:15,032
For those who become pregnant, long-term maternal survival rates are not adversely affected (Averette, 1999; Lambertini, 2019).

570
01:12:15,032 --> 01:12:25,557
One metaanalysis found that for women with early breast cancer, pregnancy that occurs 10 months after diagnosis may, in fact, confer a survival benefit .

571
01:12:25,557 --> 01:12:29,032
Breastfeeding does not adversely alter the course.

572
01:12:29,032 --> 01:12:34,032
In women successfully treated for breast cancer, recurrence is a concern.

573
01:12:34,032 --> 01:12:41,682
Because recurrences are more common soon after treatment, it seems reasonable to delay conception for 2 to 3 years.

574
01:12:41,682 --> 01:12:49,607
Hormonal contraceptive methods are contraindicated, and a copper-containing intrauterine device is an excellent method for many.

575
01:12:49,607 --> 01:12:56,482
That said, women with breast cancer who subsequently conceive do not appear to have diminished survival rates .

576
01:12:56,482 --> 01:13:02,982
Those who developed breast cancer within 10 years of delivery have and increased risk for metastases .

577
01:13:02,982 --> 01:13:09,782
Importantly, tamoxifen, which may be used long-term following initial therapy, is a teratogen.

578
01:13:09,782 --> 01:13:14,269
Discontinuation 2 months prior to conception is recommended .

579
01:13:14,269 --> 01:13:27,532
BRCA1/2 MUTATIONS Hereditary breast and ovarian cancer (HBOC) syndrome yields a susceptibility to either one or both of these two cancers in individuals with recognized gene mutations .

580
01:13:27,532 --> 01:13:33,744
BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutations are preeminent, but others are associated.

581
01:13:33,744 --> 01:13:36,369
Table 66-2.

582
01:13:36,369 --> 01:13:38,219
Some Genes

583
01:13:38,380 --> 01:13:48,467
Associated with Hereditary Cancers Preventively, cancer screening, chemoprevention, prophylactic surgery, and preimplantation testing are options.

584
01:13:48,417 --> 01:13:56,167
First, ovarian cancer screening with TVS or serum CA125 levels is not routinely recommended .

585
01:13:56,167 --> 01:14:09,067
For breast cancer, surveillance in those aged 25 to 29 years is clinical breast examination (CBE) performed by a provider once or twice yearly plus annual breast MR imaging.

586
01:14:09,067 --> 01:14:15,530
For older individuals, yearly MR imaging and mammography are alternated every 6 months.

587
01:14:15,530 --> 01:14:26,705
For women with BRCA1 and BRCA2 gene mutation, combination oral contraceptives (COC) are recognized chemoprevention for ovarian cancer .

588
01:14:26,705 --> 01:14:34,105
COC effects on breast cancer risk are conflicting, and studies show no risk or modest increased risk .

589
01:14:34,105 --> 01:14:41,505
For breast cancer chemoprevention, tamoxifen can lower cancer risk in those with BRCA2 defects .

590
01:14:41,505 --> 01:14:56,705
Prophylactic bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy (BSO) is recommended after childbearing in those aged 35 to 40 years with BRCA1 defects and aged 40 to 45 years in those with BRCA2 mutations .

591
01:14:56,705 --> 01:15:08,017
BSO or mastectomy also decreases breast cancer risk in these women (Kotsopoulos, 2016; Li, 2016; Rebbeck, 2009).

592
01:15:08,017 --> 01:15:13,680
BRCA1/2 genes are transmitted in an autosomal dominant fashion.

593
01:15:13,680 --> 01:15:20,592
In those planning pregnancy, affected women may elect preimplantation genetic testing of blastocysts .

594
01:15:20,592 --> 01:15:30,492
However, with an established pregnancy, prenatal testing poses ethical concerns regarding pregnancy termination for a mutation that may not lead to cancer.

595
01:15:30,492 --> 01:15:41,017
Currently, testing for conditions that do not accrue until adulthood are discouraged by the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (2020a,b).

596
01:15:41,017 --> 01:15:56,442
Regarding parity, protective benefits for breast cancer in women with either BRCA defect show conflicting data (Kotsopoulos, 2018; Pan 2014; Rieder, 2015; Toss, 2017).

597
01:15:56,442 --> 01:16:04,117
For ovarian cancer, parity lowers rates for women with BRCA1 but not BRCA2 mutations .

598
01:16:04,117 --> 01:16:11,017
Women with either BRCA mutation who undergo induced abortion do not have an elevated breast cancer risk .

599
01:16:11,017 --> 01:16:19,505
Breastfeeding conveys a protective effect against breast cancer in those with BRCA1 defects but not BRCA2 mutations.

600
01:16:19,505 --> 01:16:26,955
It lowers ovarian cancer rates for those with either mutation (Kotsopoulos, 2012; 2020).

601
01:16:26,955 --> 01:16:37,480
Among those with either BRCA mutation, a breast cancer diagnosis during pregnancy does not lower survival rates compared with similarly affected but not pregnant women .

602
01:16:37,480 --> 01:16:46,642
After breast cancer treatment, women with either BRCA defect who pursue pregnancy do not experience increase pregnancy complication rates.

603
01:16:46,642 --> 01:16:55,742
Moreover, disease-free or overall survival rates are not worsened (Lambertini, 2020; Valentini, 2013).

604
01:16:55,742 --> 01:16:57,742
Thyroid Cancer.

605
01:16:57,742 --> 01:17:07,592
Palpable thyroid nodules are detected in 4 to 7 percent of the population, and management is found in Chapter 61 (p. 1098).

606
01:17:07,592 --> 01:17:10,780
Approximately 10 percent are malignant .

607
01:17:10,780 --> 01:17:21,567
In pregnancy, thyroid cancer incidence approximates 10 cases per 100,000 births (Spiegel, 2019; Sullivan, 2019).

608
01:17:21,567 --> 01:17:26,267
With this diagnosis, pregnancy termination is not necessary.

609
01:17:26,267 --> 01:17:32,717
Primary therapy is partial or subtotal thyroidectomy ideally done during the second trimester.

610
01:17:32,717 --> 01:17:37,817
Most lesions are well differentiated, and delayed treatment is acceptable .

611
01:17:37,817 --> 01:17:42,980
For aggressive tumors, however, prompt surgical treatment is recommended.

612
01:17:42,980 --> 01:17:46,842
Postoperatively, replacement thyroxine is given.

613
01:17:46,842 --> 01:17:50,605
A higher risk for VTE is reported for these women .

614
01:17:50,605 --> 01:17:57,155
In some thyroid cancer types, radioiodine is used for primary or postoperative treatment.

615
01:17:57,155 --> 01:18:02,542
This is contraindicated in both pregnancy and lactation for several reasons.

616
01:18:02,542 --> 01:18:11,355
First, iodine-131 transferred transplacentally is avidly trapped by the fetal thyroid gland to cause hypothyroidism.

617
01:18:11,355 --> 01:18:17,542
Second, during lactation, the breast also concentrates a substantial amount of iodide.

618
01:18:17,542 --> 01:18:26,642
This may pose neonatal risk due to radioiodine-contaminated milk ingestion and raise maternal cancer risk from significant breast irradiation.

619
01:18:26,642 --> 01:18:35,792
To limit maternal exposure, a delay of 3 months between lactation and thyroid ablation will more reliably ensure complete breast involution .

620
01:18:35,792 --> 01:18:44,717
In women with thyroid cancer who ultimately receive iodine-131 doses, pregnancy should be avoided for 6 months to 1 year.

621
01:18:44,717 --> 01:18:46,855
This time ensures

622
01:18:47,020 --> 01:18:52,020
thyroid function stability and permits confirmation of cancer remission .

623
01:18:51,970 --> 01:18:53,807
Lymphomas.

624
01:18:53,807 --> 01:18:56,345
# Hodgkin Disease.

625
01:18:56,345 --> 01:19:04,432
This lymphoma is probably B-cell derived and is cytologically distinguished from other lymphomas by Reed–Sternberg cells.

626
01:19:04,432 --> 01:19:13,707
Of cancers in pregnancy, lymphomas are common, and gestational rates are rising because of delayed childbearing (see Fig. 66-1) .

627
01:19:13,707 --> 01:19:22,957
In one review from the Nationwide Inpatient Sample, the incidence of Hodgkin lymphoma approximates 1 case in 12,400 births .

628
01:19:22,957 --> 01:19:33,707
In more than 70 percent of these cases, lymph nodes painlessly enlarge at sites above the diaphragm, that is, in the axillary, cervical, or submandibular chains.

629
01:19:33,707 --> 01:19:40,432
Approximately one third of patients have fever, night sweats, malaise, weight loss, or pruritus.

630
01:19:40,432 --> 01:19:45,095
Diagnosis is by histological examination of involved nodes .

631
01:19:45,095 --> 01:19:49,995
The Lugano staging system is applied to Hodgkin and other lymphomas .

632
01:19:49,995 --> 01:20:02,682
For staging, pregnancy limits the use of some radiographic studies, but at minimum, chest radiography, abdominal imaging with sonography or MR imaging, and bone marrow biopsy are completed .

633
01:20:02,682 --> 01:20:08,957
MR imaging is excellent for evaluating thoracic and abdominal paraaortic lymph nodes.

634
01:20:08,957 --> 01:20:11,545
Table 66-3.

635
01:20:11,545 --> 01:20:22,632
Lugano Classification Staging System for Hodgkin and Other Lymphomas The current trend for nonpregnant individuals is to administer chemotherapy for all stages of Hodgkin disease.

636
01:20:22,632 --> 01:20:38,195
In pregnancy, for early-stage disease in the first trimester, options include pregnancy termination or observation until after 12 weeks’ gestation and then multiagent chemotherapy (Eyre, 2015; McCormick, 2018).

637
01:20:38,195 --> 01:20:47,457
For most advanced-stage disease after the first trimester, cycles of doxorubicin, bleomycin, vinblastine, and dacarbazine are given.

638
01:20:47,457 --> 01:20:56,232
In general, postponement of therapy until fetal maturity is achieved seems justifiable only when the diagnosis is made late in pregnancy.

639
01:20:56,232 --> 01:21:05,020
Women with Hodgkin lymphoma have a higher incidence of VTE (ElMessidi, 2015; Horowitz, 2016).

640
01:21:05,020 --> 01:21:13,157
Also, in our experiences, the gravidas— even after they are “cured”—are inordinately susceptible to infection and sepsis.

641
01:21:13,157 --> 01:21:17,807
Active antineoplastic therapy only raises this vulnerability.

642
01:21:17,807 --> 01:21:26,707
The overall prognosis with Hodgkin lymphoma is similar to that for nonpregnant women, and 5-year survival rates exceed 90 percent .

643
01:21:26,707 --> 01:21:35,007
Pregnancy does not adversely affect the cancer course of this lymphoma, and pregnancy outcomes are not generally adversely affected.

644
01:21:35,007 --> 01:21:40,207
For women with disease in remission, pregnancy does not stimulate relapse .

645
01:21:40,207 --> 01:21:43,170
# Non-Hodgkin Lymphomas.

646
01:21:43,170 --> 01:21:50,670
Although usually B-cell tumors, non-Hodgkin lymphomas can also be T-cell or natural-killer-cell neoplasms.

647
01:21:50,670 --> 01:21:55,182
Their biology, classification, and treatment are complex.

648
01:21:55,182 --> 01:22:05,920
They are associated with viral infections, and their incidence has risen sharply at least partly because 5 to 10 percent of persons with HIV infection develop lymphoma.

649
01:22:05,920 --> 01:22:13,045
Other associated viruses include Epstein-Barr and hepatitis C viruses and human herpes virus 8.

650
01:22:13,045 --> 01:22:19,320
Some of these lymphomas are aggressive, and survival rates vary with the type of cell line involved.

651
01:22:19,320 --> 01:22:23,307
Non-Hodgkin lymphomas are infrequent during pregnancy .

652
01:22:23,307 --> 01:22:26,932
They also are staged according to the Lugano system.

653
01:22:26,932 --> 01:22:36,982
If diagnosed in the first trimester, pregnancy termination followed by multiagent chemotherapy is recommended for all but indolent or very early disease.

654
01:22:36,982 --> 01:22:43,757
These less aggressive forms may be observed in the first trimester, and then full treatment given in the second.

655
01:22:43,757 --> 01:22:54,295
One regimen is rituximab plus the CHOP combination of cyclophosphamide, doxorubicin (hydroxydaunorubicin), vincristine [Oncovin], and prednisone.

656
01:22:54,295 --> 01:23:01,670
In a study of 80 pregnant women with this regimen, the 3-year survival rate was 73 to 96 percent .

657
01:23:01,670 --> 01:23:07,782
Burkitt lymphoma is an aggressive B-cell tumor associated with EpsteinBarr virus infection.

658
01:23:07,782 --> 01:23:12,407
Prognosis is poor, and treatment is multiagent chemotherapy.

659
01:23:12,407 --> 01:23:20,870
In an earlier review of 19 women whose pregnancies were complicated by this lymphoma, 17 died within a year of diagnosis .

660
01:23:20,870 --> 01:23:23,207
# Leukemias.

661
01:23:23,207 --> 01:23:33,170
These malignancies generally arise either from lymphoid tissues— lymphoblastic or lymphocytic leukemias, or from bone marrow—myeloid leukemias.

662
01:23:33,170 --> 01:23:35,382
They can be acute or

663
01:23:35,548 --> 01:23:37,085
chronic.

664
01:23:37,035 --> 01:23:46,335
Adult leukemias are more prevalent after age 40 but still are among the most common malignancies of young women (see Fig. 66-1).

665
01:23:46,335 --> 01:23:55,885
In two large registries, the incidence was 1 case in 40,000 to 50,000 births (Nolan, 2020; Smith, 2003).

666
01:23:55,885 --> 01:24:10,873
In a review of 72 pregnancies complicated by leukemia from 1975 until 1988, 44 had acute myelogenous leukemia; 20 had acute lymphocytic leukemia; and eight had one of the chronic leukemias .

667
01:24:10,873 --> 01:24:15,548
Nolan and colleagues (2020) cite similar proportions.

668
01:24:15,548 --> 01:24:26,910
Acute leukemias almost always cause marked peripheral blood count abnormalities, and often the white blood cell count is elevated with readily recognizable circulating blast cells.

669
01:24:26,910 --> 01:24:30,585
The diagnosis is made from bone marrow biopsy.

670
01:24:30,585 --> 01:24:39,073
With current multiagent chemotherapy, remission during pregnancy is common, and termination does not further improve the prognosis.

671
01:24:39,073 --> 01:24:46,285
In some cases, pregnancy termination before viability may simplify management of an acutely ill woman.

672
01:24:46,285 --> 01:24:52,623
Abortion is a consideration in early pregnancy to avoid potential chemotherapy teratogens.

673
01:24:52,623 --> 01:25:03,010
One is all-trans-retinoic acid, also known as tretinoin, which causes retinoic acid syndrome (Li, 2020; Santolaria, 2020).

674
01:25:03,010 --> 01:25:09,048
Tyrosine kinase inhibitors are another teratogenic group (p. 1163) .

675
01:25:09,048 --> 01:25:15,435
Other than these caveats, treatment of gravidas with leukemia is similar to that for nonpregnant women.

676
01:25:15,435 --> 01:25:19,323
Acute myeloid leukemia is treated without delay .

677
01:25:19,323 --> 01:25:29,398
After induction chemotherapy, postremission maintenance therapy is mandatory to prevent a relapse, which is then usually treated with stem-cell transplantation.

678
01:25:29,398 --> 01:25:35,385
If allogeneic stem-cell transplantation is indicated, early delivery is considered.

679
01:25:35,385 --> 01:25:41,260
With some chronic leukemias, it may be possible to delay therapy until after delivery .

680
01:25:41,260 --> 01:25:49,310
As with lymphoma, infection and hemorrhage are significant complications that should be anticipated in women with active disease.

681
01:25:49,310 --> 01:25:59,373
Most descriptions of leukemia treatment in pregnancy are single cases or small series (Routledge, 2018; Sanz, 2015).

682
01:25:59,373 --> 01:26:05,848
In one review of 58 cases, 75 percent were diagnosed after the first trimester .

683
01:26:05,848 --> 01:26:12,785
Half were acute myelogenous leukemia, which had a remission rate of 75 percent with chemotherapy.

684
01:26:12,785 --> 01:26:17,248
Only 40 percent of these pregnancies resulted in a live birth .

685
01:26:17,248 --> 01:26:25,485
In a more recent report of 92 pregnant women with acute promyelocytic leukemia, 91 percent had a complete remission .

686
01:26:25,485 --> 01:26:27,660
Malignant Melanoma.

687
01:26:27,660 --> 01:26:32,573
These most often originate from melanocytes in a preexisting nevus.

688
01:26:32,573 --> 01:26:38,310
Lesions most often develop in fair-skinned whites and commonly in childbearingaged women.

689
01:26:38,310 --> 01:26:46,160
Pigmented lesions that change in contour or height or show discoloration, bleeding, or ulceration should prompt biopsy .

690
01:26:46,160 --> 01:26:57,135
In some population studies, melanoma is the most frequent malignancy complicating pregnancy (Andersson, 2015; Bannister-Tyrrell, 2015).

691
01:26:57,135 --> 01:27:06,248
The reported incidence ranges from <1 to 3 cases per 1000 births (Cottreau, 2019; Eibye, 2013).

692
01:27:06,248 --> 01:27:11,148
Many are treated outpatient and thus not entered into tumor registries.

693
01:27:11,148 --> 01:27:13,410
Staging is clinical.

694
01:27:13,410 --> 01:27:23,573
Stage I is a melanoma with no palpable lymph nodes; in stage II, lymph nodes are palpable; and in stage III, distant metastases are identified.

695
01:27:23,573 --> 01:27:29,760
For patients with stage I, tumor thickness is the single most important predictor of survival.

696
01:27:29,760 --> 01:27:37,873
The Clark classification includes five levels of involvement by depth into the epidermis, dermis, and subcutaneous fat.

697
01:27:37,873 --> 01:27:43,435
The Breslow scale measures tumor thickness and size, in addition to invasion depth.

698
01:27:43,435 --> 01:27:53,423
Primary surgical treatment for melanoma is determined by the stage and includes wide local resection, sometimes with extensive regional lymph node dissection.

699
01:27:53,423 --> 01:28:09,648
The American Academy of Dermatology recommends sentinel lymph node mapping and biopsy using technetium-99m–sulfur colloid, which has a calculated fetal dose of 0.014 mSv or 0.014 mGy .

700
01:28:09,648 --> 01:28:17,523
Routine regional node dissection reportedly improves survival rates in nonpregnant patients with microscopic metastases.

701
01:28:17,523 --> 01:28:28,323
For gravidas, an algorithm is proposed that begins with resection of the primary tumor under local anesthesia but postpones sentinel lymph node biopsy until postpartum .

702
01:28:28,323 --> 01:28:32,710
Although prophylactic chemotherapy or immunotherapy is

703
01:28:32,860 --> 01:28:39,847
usually avoided during pregnancy, it may be given if indicated by tumor stage and maternal prognosis.

704
01:28:39,797 --> 01:28:45,422
In most cases of distant metastatic melanoma, treatment is at best palliative.

705
01:28:45,422 --> 01:28:55,110
Stage-for-stage, survival is equivalent between pregnant and nonpregnant women (Driscoll, 2016; Johansson, 2014).

706
01:28:55,110 --> 01:29:03,797
In two studies, half of pregnant women presented with an advanced stage (de Haan, 2017; Sawyers, 2020).

707
01:29:03,797 --> 01:29:10,872
Placentas are submitted for histological evaluation to exclude metastasis (p. 1164).

708
01:29:10,872 --> 01:29:15,272
Therapeutic abortion does not improve maternal survival rates.

709
01:29:15,272 --> 01:29:24,710
Clinical stage is the strongest determinant of survival, and women with deep cutaneous invasion or regional node involvement have the worst prognosis.

710
01:29:24,710 --> 01:29:32,060
Approximately 60 percent of recurrences will manifest within 2 years, and 90 percent by 5 years.

711
01:29:32,060 --> 01:29:38,660
Thus, most recommend that pregnancy be avoided for 3 to 5 years after surgical resection.

712
01:29:38,660 --> 01:29:46,547
Interim contraception can include combination oral contraceptives, as they do not appear to have adverse cancer effects .

713
01:29:46,547 --> 01:29:49,435
Gastrointestinal Tract Cancer.

714
01:29:49,435 --> 01:29:55,960
Carcinomas of the colon and rectum are the third most frequent cancer in all women in the United States .

715
01:29:55,960 --> 01:30:00,560
Their incidence in pregnancy is rising because of delayed childbearing .

716
01:30:00,560 --> 01:30:05,335
Even so, colorectal tumors are uncommon before age 40.

717
01:30:05,335 --> 01:30:13,010
An approximate incidence of 1 case in 150,000 deliveries was derived from the California Cancer Registry .

718
01:30:13,010 --> 01:30:19,635
In another report, however, the incidence approximated 1 case in 13,000 pregnancies .

719
01:30:19,635 --> 01:30:25,160
Of colorectal carcinomas in pregnant women, 80 percent arise from the rectum.

720
01:30:25,160 --> 01:30:32,647
In one review, only 41 cases in pregnancy were colon cancers located above the peritoneal reflection .

721
01:30:32,647 --> 01:30:39,585
The most frequent symptoms are abdominal pain, distention, nausea, constipation, and rectal bleeding.

722
01:30:39,585 --> 01:30:47,910
If symptoms of colon disease persist, digital rectal examination, stool tests for occult blood, and colonoscopy are done.

723
01:30:47,910 --> 01:30:54,297
Some gastrointestinal (GI) tract cancers are found because of metastases to the ovary.

724
01:30:54,297 --> 01:31:02,272
These Krukenberg tumors are tumor-laden ovaries from another, often GI, primary and carry a bleak prognosis .

725
01:31:02,272 --> 01:31:06,910
Colon cancer treatment in gravidas mirrors that for nonpregnant women.

726
01:31:06,910 --> 01:31:14,822
Without evidence of metastatic disease, surgical resection is preferred, but most pregnant women have advanced lesions .

727
01:31:14,822 --> 01:31:24,860
During the first half of pregnancy, hysterectomy is not necessary to perform colon or rectal resection, and thus, therapeutic abortion is not mandated.

728
01:31:24,860 --> 01:31:30,085
During later pregnancy, therapy may be delayed until fetal maturation.

729
01:31:30,085 --> 01:31:36,085
However, bowel hemorrhage, obstruction, or perforation may force surgical intervention.

730
01:31:36,085 --> 01:31:40,222
Gastric and esophageal cancers are rare in pregnancy.

731
01:31:40,222 --> 01:31:48,485
Despite this, persistent unexplained upper GI symptoms should be prompt upper abdominal sonography and perhaps endoscopy.

